= [...], idx=0. Each motionDt: move toward path[idx]; if reached end → complete. Stall detection.\n- WAIT_AT_PANEL: {floor, dir, toFloor}. Press call each frame (world.floors[floor].callPanel.setUp/setDown). Stand at panel node position? The agent should stand near the panel; plan compiler precedes with WALK_TO_WP(elevWait). So during WAIT_AT_PANEL, agent stands at its current position (or walks to elevWait if not there). Condition: elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor, dir) && capacity free → complete. Then next action ENTER_ELEVATOR.\n- ENTER_ELEVATOR: {toFloor}. phases: 'reserve' → reserveBoardingSpot(agent); if null re-press call; else store spot. phase 'walkDoor': walk to door threshold world position (x = spot.x, z = car front). Then reparent group from scene (or buildingGroup) to car group at car-local coords. phase 'walkSpot': move in car-local space to spot; then completeBoard → complete.\n  Need agent.carLocal position: after reparenting, agent.group.parent = elevator.carGroup and set local position = spot coords. World pos preserved: use `elevator.carGroup.worldToLocal(worldPos)`.\n- PRESS_FLOOR: pressDestination(floor); light button; complete immediately.\n- WAIT_FOR_FLOOR: until elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===floor.\n- EXIT_ELEVATOR: {toFloor}: registerDisembark, reparent car→scene at world position (walk to door threshold inside car first), then walk to elevWait node on that floor, completeDisembark → complete.\n  Order per spec: \"reparent car -> scene (preserving world pos, and registerDisembark to hold the doors); walk to elevWait; completeDisembark.\" So: at start of EXIT_ELEVATOR, agent is inside car at spot; must first walk to door threshold then step out. I'll do: phase 'walkDoor' in car-local space toward (spot.x, 0, front edge z≈1.2), then reparent to scene, registerDisembark at the start (to hold doors) — yes register immediately at start so doors stay open. Then walk to elevWait node, then completeDisembark.\n- SIT: target sitTargets