his.currentFloor) return false;\n    if (direction === 0 || this.direction === 0 || direction === this.direction) return true;\n    // caller wants opposite direction: only accept if no stops pending in current direction\n    return !this.hasStopsAhead(this.direction);\n}\n```\n\nhasStopsAhead(dir): any destination or matching call strictly ahead in dir.\n\ncurrentCapacityFree(): maxCapacity - (passengers.size + pendingBoarders.size).\n\nreserveBoardingSpot(person): if capacity free, find first unoccupied spot index, mark occupancy with person, add to pendingBoarders, return {index,x,y,z}. Return null if full.\n\ncompleteBoard(person): pendingBoarders.delete; passengers.add; keep spot occupancy (spotOccupancy[person._spotIndex]) — need mapping. Store `person._spot` when reserving? Better: maintain a Map person→spotIndex. Use `this.spotOf = new Map()`. In completeBoard, keep mapping. On completeDisembark, release spot & delete mapping.\n\nregisterDisembark(person): pendingDisembark.add(person).\ncompleteDisembark(person): pendingDisembark.delete; passengers.delete; release spot.\n\ntick(dt): as described.\n\nAt DOOR_OPEN arrival: serveFloor() — clear destinations for that floor; clear hall call for current direction; if no more stops in current direction, also clear opposite-direction call at this floor. Also set servedThisDoorCycle = true, reopenedAtSameFloor=false.\n\nHmm careful with test 1: after boarding 4 and pressing destinations, doors close → pickTarget must be above 0. ✓.\n\nAlso important: when car is full (passengers+pendingBoarders == max) at floor 0 with leftover calls at 0 — during DOOR_OPEN, pending boarders complete → doors close; then pick target = destination ✓.\n\nNow the \"no same-floor reopen\" rule in pickTarget: exclude currentFloor if passengers.size>0 || destinations.size>0. If nothing else and car empty and call at current floor exists → we can serve (reopen) but guard with reopenedAtSameFloor flag to prevent infinite loop... Actually if car is empty at floor 0 with an up call, opening doors again is correct behavior (new waiters). The guard is only \"while destinations exist\". I'll implement:\n\n```js\npickTarget() {\n    const cur = this.currentFloor;\n    if (this.destinations.size > 0) { ... } // never returns cur because destinations for cur were cleared at arrival\n    // calls in current direction ahead\n    let best = scanCalls(cur, this.direction);\n    if (best !== null) return best;\n    if (this.passengers.size === 0 && this.destinations.size === 0) {\n        const other = scanCalls(cur, -this.direction);\n        if (other !== null) { this.direction = -this.direction; return other; }\n        // same floor call: allow reopen once per cycle\n        if (!this.reopenedAtSameFloor && hasCallAt(cur)) { return cur; }\n    }\n    const anyNearest = nearestAnyStop(); ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, careful with test 4 (opposite-direction calls wait their turn): while moving UP with work above, a DOWN call at current or lower floor should not reverse until upward destinations/calls served. Our tick during MOVING re-evaluates target: scan for closer stop in same direction only ✓; don't switch to opposite direction mid-trip unless no work ahead? Spec says \"Re-evaluate target during MOVING: each frame, scan for a closer stop in the same direction and shorten targetFloor if appropriate.\" So no reversal mid-trip ✓.\n\nAt door-close transition after serving, pickTarget prefers current direction; if none ahead, reverse → that's fine (test 4 asserts while work above exists, doesn't reverse).\n\nNow, during MOVING re-evaluation: also consider destinations in same direction closer than target ✓ and calls matching direction ahead.\n\nLet me write scan function `scanAhead(dir)` returning nearest stop floor in dir direction (destinations outrank calls? For simplicity, pick nearest stop; but rule says passenger destinations outrank same-floor hall calls — that's about reopening). I'll implement: prefer destinations in direction; else calls in direction.\n\nImplementation of pickTarget with priority:\n1. If destinations.size>0 → nearest destination ahead in current dir; if none, nearest destination anywhere (reverse).\n2. Else scan calls in current dir ahead; if found return.\n3. Else scan calls behind (reverse) — but only when car empty? Real elevators reverse for calls. Test 4 requires not reversing while upward work exists — covered by step 2 finding work. If no work ahead and there's a down call below, reversing is correct.\n4. Else same-floor guard.\n\nAlso handle direction inference when idle: pick nearest active call/destination overall and infer direction.\n\nNow door timers & state transitions. Also `doorOpenFraction` for visual adapter (0..1). I'll track `this.doorProgress` = 0 closed, 1 open; updated during OPENING/CLOSING over doorTravelS.\n\nLet me write the file.\n\nAlso expose `stateList`? Not needed.\n\nEdge: when state IDLE and there are calls at current floor → should we open doors? Yes: in tick IDLE branch, if hasCallAt(currentFloor) or destinations.has(currentFloor) → transition to DOOR_OPENING (with servedThisDoorCycle guard). Otherwise pick target & move.\n\nLet me write it now.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now the pure elevator logic — the authoritative brain.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"xRNx3M50nNXBNCfeMgOdvZtYmyG6zgXR","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// elevator_logic.js - pure elevator scheduler / state machine.\n// No Three.js, DOM, canvas or browser-only dependencies so it runs under Node too.\n\n(function (root) {\n    const IDLE = \"IDLE\";\n    const MOVING = \"MOVING\";\n    const DOOR_OPENING = \"DOOR_OPENING\";\n    const DOOR_OPEN = \"DOOR_OPEN\";\n    const DOOR_CLOSING = \"DOOR_CLOSING\";\n\n    const STATES = [IDLE, MOVING, DOOR_OPENING, DOOR_OPEN, DOOR_CLOSING];\n\n    function defaultSpots() {\n        // Four logical interior spots, car-local coordinates (car floor at y = 0).\n        return [\n            { index: 0, x: -0.72, y: 0, z: -0.55 },\n            { index: 1, x: 0.72, y: 0, z: -0.55 },\n            { index: 2, x: -0.72, y: 0, z: 0.45 },\n            { index: 3, x: 0.72, y: 0, z: 0.45 }\n        ];\n    }\n\n    class ElevatorLogic {\n        constructor(options) {\n            const opts = options || {};\n            this.floorCount = opts.floorCount !== undefined ? opts.floorCount : 6;\n            this.maxCapacity = opts.maxCapacity !== undefined ? opts.maxCapacity : 4;\n            this.floorHeight = opts.floorHeight !== undefined ? opts.floorHeight : 3.4;\n\n            this.minDoorOpenS = opts.minDoorOpenS !== undefined ? opts.minDoorOpenS : 2.5;\n            this.maxDoorOpenS = opts.maxDoorOpenS !== undefined ? opts.maxDoorOpenS : 10;\n            this.doorTravelS = opts.doorTravelS !== undefined ? opts.doorTravelS : 0.8;\n            this.floorsPerSecond = opts.floorsPerSecond !== undefined ? opts.floorsPerSecond : 1.6;\n\n            this.spots = defaultSpots();\n\n            this.upCalls = new Set();\n            this.downCalls = new Set();\n            this.destinations = new Set();\n            this.passengers = new Set();\n            this.pendingBoarders = new Set();\n            this.pendingDisembark = new Set();\n            this.spotOf = new Map();\n\n            this.reset();\n        }\n\n        reset() {\n            this.upCalls.clear();\n            this.downCalls.clear();\n            this.destinations.clear();\n            this.passengers.clear();\n            this.pendingBoarders.clear();\n            this.pendingDisembark.clear();\n            this.spotOf.clear();\n            for (let i = 0; i < this.spots.length; i += 1) {\n                this.spots[i].occupant = null;\n            }\n\n            this.state = IDLE;\n            this.direction = 0;\n            this.currentFloor = 0;\n            this.targetFloor = 0;\n            this.carPos = 0;\n            this.doorProgress = 0;\n            this.doorTimer = 0;\n            this.doorOpenElapsed = 0;\n            this.servedThisDoorCycle = false;\n            this.lastServedFloor = -1;\n            this.reopenedAtSameFloor = false;\n        }\n\n        inRange(floor) {\n            return floor >= 0 && floor < this.floorCount;\n        }\n\n        callUp(floor) {\n            if (this.inRange(floor)) this.upCalls.add(floor);\n        }\n\n        callDown(floor) {\n            if (this.inRange(floor)) this.downCalls.add(floor);\n        }\n\n        pressDestination(floor) {\n            if (this.inRange(floor)) this.destinations.add(floor);\n        }\n\n        hasCallAt(floor) {\n            return this.upCalls.has(floor) || this.downCalls.has(floor);\n        }\n\n        currentCapacityFree() {\n            return this.maxCapacity - (this.passengers.size + this.pendingBoarders.size);\n        }\n\n        reserveBoardingSpot(person) {\n            if (this.currentCapacityFree() <= 0) return null;\n            for (let i = 0; i < this.spots.length; i += 1) {\n                if (!this.spots[i].occupant) {\n                    this.spots[i].occupant = person;\n                    this.spotOf.set(person, i);\n                    this.pendingBoarders.add(person);\n                    return { index: i, x: this.spots[i].x, y: this.spots[i].y, z: this.spots[i].z };\n                }\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n\n        completeBoard(person) {\n            const spotIndex = this.spotOf.get(person);\n            if (spotIndex === undefined) return false;\n            this.pendingBoarders.delete(person);\n            this.passengers.add(person);\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        registerDisembark(person) {\n            this.pendingDisembark.add(person);\n        }\n\n        completeDisembark(person) {\n            this.pendingDisembark.delete(person);\n            this.passengers.delete(person);\n            const spotIndex = this.spotOf.get(person);\n            if (spotIndex !== undefined) {\n                this.spots[spotIndex].occupant = null;\n                this.spotOf.delete(person);\n            }\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        spotFor(person) {\n            const index = this.spotOf.get(person);\n            if (index === undefined) return null;\n            const spot = this.spots[index];\n            return { index: spot.index, x: spot.x, y: spot.y, z: spot.z };\n        }\n\n        // True only when the car is at `floor` in DOOR_OPEN and either there are no\n        // more stops pending in the current direction, or the caller's direction matches.\n        isAcceptingAt(floor, direction) {\n            if (this.state !== DOOR_OPEN || floor !== this.currentFloor) return false;\n            if (direction === 0 || this.direction === 0 || direction === this.direction) return true;\n            return !this.hasStopsAhead(this.direction);\n        }\n\n        hasStopsAhead(dir) {\n            if (dir === 0) return false;\n            for (const dest of this.destinations) {\n                if ((dest - this.currentFloor) * dir > 0) return true;\n            }\n            const calls = dir > 0 ? this.upCalls : this.downCalls;\n            for (const floor of calls) {\n                if ((floor - this.currentFloor) * dir > 0) return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        // Nearest stop strictly ahead in `dir`; passenger destinations outrank hall calls.\n        scanAhead(dir) {\n            if (dir === 0) return null;\n            let bestDest = null;\n            let bestCall = null;\n            for (const dest of this.destinations) {\n                if ((dest - this.currentFloor) * dir <= 0) continue;\n                if (bestDest === null || Math.abs(dest - this.currentFloor) < Math.abs(bestDest - this.currentFloor)) {\n                    bestDest = dest;\n                }\n            }\n            const calls = dir > 0 ? this.upCalls : this.downCalls;\n            for (const floor of calls) {\n                if ((floor - this.currentFloor) * dir <= 0) continue;\n                if (bestCall === null || Math.abs(floor - this.currentFloor) < Math.abs(bestCall - this.currentFloor)) {\n                    bestCall = floor;\n                }\n            }\n            if (bestDest !== null) return bestDest;\n            return bestCall;\n        }\n\n        nearestAnywhere() {\n            let best = null;\n            const consider = (floor) => {\n                if (!this.inRange(floor)) return;\n                if (best === null || Math.abs(floor - this.currentFloor) < Math.abs(best - this.currentFloor)) best = floor;\n            };\n            for (const dest of this.destinations) consider(dest);\n            for (const floor of this.upCalls) consider(floor);\n            for (const floor of this.downCalls) consider(floor);\n            return best;\n        }\n\n        // Target selection at the door-close -> pick-next-target transition.\n        pickTarget() {\n            const cur = this.currentFloor;\n\n            if (this.destinations.size > 0) {\n                let ahead = scanAheadIn(this.destinations, this.direction);\n                if (ahead === null) {\n                    for (const dest of this.destinations) {\n                        if (dest === cur) continue;\n                        ahead = pickNearest(this.destinations, cur);\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (ahead !== null && ahead !== cur) return ahead;\n            }\n\n            // Hall calls in the current direction first.\n            let target = scanAhead(this.direction);\n            if (target !== null && target !== cur) return target;\n\n            // Nothing left ahead -> reverse and look behind.\n            const behind = scanAhead(-this.direction);\n            if (behind !== null && behind !== cur) {\n                this.direction = -this.direction;\n                return behind;\n            }\n\n            // Same-floor work: only allowed once per door cycle, and never while riders\n            // still have destinations (that is the classic lobby-starvation bug).\n            if (!this.servedThisDoorCycle || !this.reopenedAtSameFloor) {\n                if (hasWorkAnywhere(this)) {\n                    const nearest = nearestAnywhere(this);\n                    if (nearest !== null && nearest !== cur) return nearest;\n                }\n                if (!this.passengers.size && !this.destinations.size && this.hasCallAt(cur)) {\n                    this.reopenedAtSameFloor = true;\n                    return cur;\n                }\n            }\n\n            const fallback = nearestAnywhere(this);\n            if (fallback !== null && fallback !== cur) return fallback;\n            return null;\n        }\n\n        serveCurrentFloor() {\n            this.destinations.delete(this.currentFloor);\n            if (this.direction > 0) {\n                this.upCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n            } else if (this.direction < 0) {\n                this.downCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n            } else {\n                this.upCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n                this.downCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n            }\n            if (!hasStopsAheadFor(this, this.direction)) {\n                // Serve the opposite-direction call at this floor before leaving.\n                if (this.direction >= 0) this.downCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n                else this.upCalls.delete(this.currentFloor);\n            }\n            this.servedThisDoorCycle = true;\n            this.lastServedFloor = this.currentFloor;\n        }\n\n        arriveAt(floor) {\n            this.currentFloor = floor;\n            this.carPos = floor;\n            this.state = DOOR_OPENING;\n            this.doorTimer = 0;\n            this.doorOpenElapsed = 0;\n            this.servedThisDoorCycle = false;\n        }\n\n        tick(dt) {\n            if (this.state === MOVING) {\n                // Re-evaluate every frame: a closer stop in the same direction shortens the trip.\n                const recheck = scanAhead(this.direction);\n                if (recheck !== null && recheck !== this.currentFloor) {\n                    if (Math.abs(recheck - this.currentFloor) < Math.abs(this.targetFloor - this.currentFloor)) {\n                        this.targetFloor = recheck;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (this.targetFloor === this.currentFloor) {\n                    this.arriveAt(this.currentFloor);\n                    return;\n                }\n                const step = this.floorsPerSecond * dt;\n                const dir = Math.sign(this.targetFloor - this.carPos);\n                this.carPos += dir * step;\n                if (Math.abs(this.carPos - this.targetFloor) <= 1e-6 || Math.sign(this.targetFloor - this.carPos) !== dir) {\n                    this.arriveAt(this.targetFloor);\n                    return;\n                }\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (this.state === DOOR_OPENING) {\n                this.doorTimer += dt;\n                this.doorProgress = Math.min(1, this.doorTimer / this.doorTravelS);\n                if (this.doorTimer >= this.doorTravelS) {\n                    this.state = DOOR_OPEN;\n                    this.doorOpenElapsed = 0;\n                    this.serveCurrentFloor();\n                }\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (this.state === DOOR_OPEN) {\n                this.doorOpenElapsed += dt;\n                const settled = this.pendingBoarders.size === 0 && this.pendingDisembark.size === 0;\n                if ((settled && this.doorOpenElapsed >= this.minDoorOpenS) || this.doorOpenElapsed >= this.maxDoorOpenS) {\n                    this.state = DOOR_CLOSING;\n                    this.doorTimer = 0;\n                }\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (this.state === DOOR_CLOSING) {\n                this.doorTimer += dt;\n                this.doorProgress = Math.max(0, 1 - this.doorTimer / this.doorTravelS);\n                if (this.doorTimer >= this.doorTravelS) {\n                    const next = this.pickTarget();\n                    this.servedThisDoorCycle = false;\n                    if (next === null || next === this.currentFloor) {\n                        this.state = IDLE;\n                        this.direction = 0;\n                        this.targetFloor = this.currentFloor;\n                        return;\n                    }\n                    this.direction = Math.sign(next - this.currentFloor);\n                    this.targetFloor = next;\n                    this.state = MOVING;\n                }\n                return;\n            }\n\n            // IDLE\n            if (this.hasCallAt(this.currentFloor) || this.destinations.has(this.currentFloor)) {\n                this.arriveAt(this.currentFloor);\n                return;\n            }\n            const next = this.pickTarget();\n            if (next === null) return;\n            this.direction = Math.sign(next - this.currentFloor);\n            this.targetFloor = next;\n            this.state = MOVING;\n        }\n\n        function scanAheadIn(set, dir) {\n            if (dir === 0) return null;\n            let best = null;\n            for (const floor of set) {\n                if ((floor - this.currentFloor) * dir <= 0) continue;\n                if (best === null || Math.abs(floor - this.currentFloor) < Math.abs(best - this.currentFloor)) best = floor;\n            }\n            return best;\n        }\n\n        displayText() {\n            const glyph = Math.round(this.carPos);\n            if (this.state === MOVING) {\n                return this.direction > 0 ? glyph + \"^\" : this.direction < 0 ? glyph + \"v\" : String(glyph);\n            }\n            return String(glyph);\n        }\n\n        doorOpenFraction() {\n            return this.doorProgress;\n        }\n    }\n\n    function pickNearest(set, from) {\n        let best = null;\n        for (const floor of set) {\n            if (best === null || Math.abs(floor - from) < Math.abs(best - from)) best = floor;\n        }\n        return best;\n    }\n\n    function hasWorkAnywhere(elevator) {\n        return elevator.destinations.size > 0 || elevator.upCalls.size > 0 || elevator.downCalls.size > 0;\n    }\n\n    function hasStopsAheadFor(elevator, dir) {\n        return elevator.hasStopsAhead(dir);\n    }\n\n    root.ElevatorLogic = ElevatorLogic;\n    if (typeof window !== \"undefined\") window.ElevatorLogic = ElevatorLogic;\n    if (typeof module !== \"undefined\" && module.exports) {\n        module.exports = { ElevatorLogic };\n    }\n})(typeof window !== \"undefined\" ? window : globalThis);\n","path":"C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/elevator_logic.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"lmstudio","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-gsq-rco","usage":{"input":44589,"output":5344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1666,"totalTokens":49933,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791655829520,"responseId":"chatcmpl-yc1du6boap2ujv24b8ol3","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1105807,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"xRNx3M50nNXBNCfeMgOdvZtYmyG6zgXR","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/elevator_logic.js"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1791656935333}]}
