{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":60704,"output":1489,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":773,"totalTokens":62193,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Interesting! The car reached floor 5 and then... \"result IDLE 0\" — currentFloor became 0?! That means something reset or the car moved down to 0. Let's see: after reaching floor 5 (destinations served), doors open at 5, up call at 0 exists → pickTarget from door close: destinations empty; scanAhead(dir=1) none; reverse → downCalls? up call at 0 is an UP call at floor 0 — not a down call. So `scanAhead(-dir)` looks for down calls below → none. Then the same-floor guard block: hasWorkAnywhere true (upCall at 0) → nearest = 0 ≠ cur(5) → return 0 → direction = -1, MOVING to floor 0 ✓ that's fine behavior. Then arrives at 0, doors open... but predicate `currentFloor>=2 && DOOR_OPEN` was checked during the run — it should have been true when doors opened at floor 2 or 3 etc. But the loop printed \"state DOOR_CLOSING floor 5\" after 200 ticks — meaning within those 200 ticks, the car went from 0 to 5 and doors opened at each stop? Let's see: 200 ticks = 20 s; travel 0→2 takes 1.25s (12.5 ticks), then door cycle ~3.3+... Actually minDoorOpenS=2.5 + door travel 0.8*2 = so each stop ~4.6s ≈ 46 ticks. 5 stops → ~230 ticks. So within 200 ticks it reached floor 5 mid-door-cycle (DOOR_CLOSING at floor 5). Then runUntil: predicate currentFloor>=2 && DOOR_OPEN — at floor 5, doors closing then... after close, pickTarget → goes to 0 (up call at 0), arrives at 0, opens doors there → predicate false (floor 0 < 2). Then it stays: at floor 0 with up call... doors open at 0 → predicate false forever since no passengers/destinations remain and the only work is the call at 0. So cap exceeded — my test's expectation was wrong because by then all destinations were served.\n\nFix test 1: assert that after door close, target > 0 (already), and then run until it opens doors at a floor ≥ 2 *before* the leftover-call loop, or check that during the re-pressing phase the car doesn't reopen floor 0 while destinations remain. Better structure:\n\n```\nrunUntil(elev, e => e.state === 'DOOR_OPEN' && e.currentFloor >= 2)   // served a rider destination\n// then assert it never reopened at floor 0 during that trip\n```\nAnd also record max floor reached. Let me restructure test 1:\n\n- open doors at 0, board 4, press destinations 2..5\n- after close: target > 0 ✓\n- then loop N ticks with re-pressing UP at 0 whenever doors are open... but careful: re-pressing while car is away; assert that the car never opens doors at floor 0 again until all destinations served. Track `reopenedLobby` flag; run until currentFloor reaches 5 (all destinations served). Assert !reopenedLobby and currentFloor===5.\n\nThat's deterministic ✓. Let me rewrite test 1 accordingly.\n\nAlso note: after serving all destinations, going to the lobby call is correct behavior.\n\nLet me update tests 1 and 6.\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":60704,"output":1489,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":773,"totalTokens":62193,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"ZUhsjtHmkSpfPbcDqEcsx2U3AGLn3wH0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\nt='elevator_logic_test.js'\ns=open(t).read()\nold = '''        assert.ok(elev.state === \"MOVING\" || elev.state === \"IDLE\", \"car should leave the lobby after doors close\");\n        assert.ok(elev.targetFloor > 0, `next target must be above floor 0 (got ${elev.targetFloor})`);\n\n        // Leftover lobby waiters keep re-pressing UP while the car is away.\n        for (let i = 0; i < 200; i += 1) {\n            elev.tick(0.1);\n            if (elev.state === \"DOOR_OPEN\") elev.callUp(0);\n        }\n\n        // The car must still serve its riders' destinations, not reopen floor 0.\n        runUntil(elev, (e) => e.currentFloor >= 2 && e.state === \"DOOR_OPEN\");\n        assert.ok(elev.currentFloor > 0, `car should have served a passenger destination (floor ${elev.currentFloor})`);'''\nnew = '''        assert.ok(elev.state === \"MOVING\" || elev.state === \"IDLE\", \"car should leave the lobby after doors close\");\n        assert.ok(elev.targetFloor > 0, `next target must be above floor 0 (got ${elev.targetFloor})`);\n\n        // Leftover lobby waiters keep re-pressing UP while the car is away. The car must\n        // still serve every rider destination before coming back to the lobby.\n        let reopenedLobby = false;\n        for (let i = 0; i < 400 && elev.destinations.size > 0; i += 1) {\n            elev.callUp(0);\n            elev.tick(0.1);\n            if (elev.state === \"DOOR_OPEN\" && elev.currentFloor === 0) reopenedLobby = true;\n        }\n\n        assert.ok(!reopenedLobby, \"car reopened the lobby while riders still had destinations\");\n        assert.strictEqual(elev.destinations.size, 0, \"passenger destinations were not served\");\n        assert.ok(elev.currentFloor >= 2, `car should be serving an upper floor (floor ${elev.currentFloor})`);'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\n\nold6 = '''        runUntilDoorClosed(elev);\n        assert.strictEqual(elev.targetFloor, toFloor, `handshake target should be ${toFloor} (got ${elev.targetFloor})`);'''\nnew6 = '''        // PRESS_FLOOR action: the exact destination from the plan compiler.\n        elev.pressDestination(rider.planToFloor);\n\n        runUntilDoorClosed(elev);\n        assert.strictEqual(elev.targetFloor, toFloor, `handshake target should be ${toFloor} (got ${elev.targetFloor})`);'''\nassert old6 in s\ns=s.replace(old6,new6)\nopen(t,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode elevator_logic_test.js"}}}}
