eserve too (unique per worker; but a visitor could take it? Visitors only go to lobby/floor lounges/conference, not office desks ✓).\n\nNow the collision & bunching concerns: agents walking along same path may overlap; soft repulsion handles.\n\nLet me think about `WALK_TO_WP` when target is on another floor — plans always include elevator ride actions between floors, so WALK_TO_WP stays within a floor ✓.\n\nAgent's current floor tracked as agent.floor.\n\nNow the top-up scheduler and dispatch loop. Let me write sim.js structure:\n\n```js\nlet scene, camera, renderer, controls;\nlet world, elevator, clock;\nconst agents = [];\nlet seatReservations = new Set();\nlet targetOccupancy = 45;\nlet hudElements...\n\nfunction startSimulation() { ...setup... createAgents(); buildHud(); animate(); }\n```\n\nClock: I'll implement as object with methods.\n\nLighting keyframes: define array `DAY_KEYS` of {h, bg:[r,g,b], sunColor, sunI, ambientI, hemiI}.\n\nNow let me think about performance: 100 agents × O(n²) collisions = 10k checks/frame — fine.\n\nHUD DOM updates each frame could be heavy; throttle to every ~0.25s real time.\n\nLet's write the code now. I'll write files one at a time, then run checkers and tests.\n\nAlso need `node elevator_logic_test.js` passing 7 scenarios.\n\nLet me start writing person.js.\n\nActually, let me consider using subagents to parallelize? The user prompt says \"Use the agentic coding tools available to you\" — that's about the eval harness (the tool being evaluated is pi). I'm the agent under evaluation. Delegating would be fine but risky for coherence; and single-writer rule. I'll write everything myself.\n\nLet me write person.js.\n\n```js\nconst PERSON_SHIRT_COLORS = [0x4a7bd6, 0xd65c4a, ...];\n```\n\nWrite code:\n\n```js\nfunction pickColor(palette) { return palette[Math.floor(Math.random() * palette.length)]; }\n\nfunction createPerson(opts) {\n    const o = opts || {};\n    const shirt = o.bodyColor !== undefined ? o.bodyColor : pickColor(PERSON_SHIRT_COLORS);\n    ...\n    const group = new THREE.Group();\n    // legs\n    const hipY = 0.82, legLen = 0.8;\n    function makeLeg(x) { const g = new THREE.Group(); g.position.set(x, hipY, 0); const m = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.1,0.09,legLen,8), matLeg); m.position.y = -legLen/2; g.add(m); group.add(g); return g; }\n```\nCareful: inner function names inside createPerson are local ✓.\n\nHead: sphere r 0.16 at y=1.62 (torso from hip 0.82 to shoulder 1.45, neck small). Nose hemisphere on +Z face of head: SphereGeometry(0.05, 8, 6) at (0, 1.66, 0.17).\n\nArms pivot at shoulder y=1.42, length 0.6 hanging below.\n\nStore references in person.userData: {legL, legR, armL, armR, walkPhase:0, isWalking:false, isSitting:false}.\n\nanimatePersonWalking(person, dt):\n```js\nfunction animatePersonWalking(person, dt) {\n  const u = person.userData;\n  if (u.isSitting) { legs -π/2, arms -π/4, walkPhase reset }\n  else if (u.isWalking) { phase += dt*8; legs sin(phase)*0.6 opposite; arms -sin(phase)*0.5 }\n  else reset to 0.\n}\n```\n\nNow world.js — big. Let me write it thoughtfully with helper functions:\n\n```js\nconst WORLD = {...};\n\nfunction makeTextTexture() { canvas 256, ctx, texture LinearFilter + generateMipmaps true + anisotropy; tex._lastText=''; }\nfunction updateTextTexture(tex) { draw tex.text... } \n```\nDesign: `createFloorDisplay(size)` returns {texture, set(text)} with cache.\n\nCall panel: group with plate box (0.55 x 1.4 x 0.05), two triangles ShapeGeometry ~0.13 half-width, canvas display 0.45 square. userData with setUp/setDown/setIndicator. Materials: dark gray unlit MeshBasicMaterial(0x2a2f36) and green emissive (0x35e07a).\n\nArrow shape: triangle pointing up for up-arrow, down for down-arrow. ShapeGeometry from THREE.Shape.\n\nPanel placement per floor: on shaft wall facing +Z at x = -1.0? Panel must be next to doors; place at (-1.2, y+1.3, 1.56). But shaft front face is z=1.5 (shaft spans -1.5..1.5); panel just outside at z=1.58 ✓ but that's inside the building interior near elevator door — fine.\n\nShaft indicator above doors: plane 0.9x0.9 at (0, y+2.6, 1.57) facing +Z.\n\nNow furniture helpers. I'll write functions with unique names to avoid cross-file collisions: `buildChair`, `buildDesk`, etc. only in world.js ✓.\n\nNode registration: `worldNodes` object per floor; helper closures inside createWorld using a local `nodes` param.\n\nLet me define structure:\n```js\nfunction createWorld(scene) {\n  const buildingGroup = new THREE.Group(); buildingGroup.renderOrder = 0; scene.add(buildingGroup);\n  const floors = [];\n  for (let f=0; f<WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT; f++) { ... }\n  return {buildingGroup, floors, bfsPath};\n}\n```\n\nNode object: `{name, pos:new THREE.Vector3(...), links:[], sit:false, facing:0}`. Store in `floor.nodes` as plain object map. bfsPath(nodes, fromName, toName) → array of Vector3.\n\nAlso expose helper `nearestNode(floorNodes, point)` global function name `worldNearestNode`.\n\nSit targets: `floor.sitTargets[wpName] = {sit:true, facing}`. For standing waypoints also entries with sit:false (spec says \"For each 'sittable' waypoint, publish a sitTargets entry\"). I'll add for all waypoints to be safe.\n\nNow sim.js needs floor lookup by index: world.floors[f].\n\nLet me write the code files now. I'll aim for correctness and completeness; then run checkers.\n\nRegarding `bfsPath` returning waypoints including start node — yes include from node, so agent walks from current pos to first node then along.\n\nNow sim.js details on walking:\n```js\nfunction walkAlongPath(agent, motionDt) {\n  const path = agent.path; if (!path.length) return true;\n  const target = path[agent.pathIndex]; ... move toward in XZ (and y snap to floor level)\n}\n```\nMovement speed: WALK_SPEED = 1.3 m/s.\n\nStall detection: track `_prevWp` position and `_stallT`.\n\nCollision: implement as described.\n\nNow, HUD state breakdown counts per state.\n\nLet me think about the ENTER_ELEVATOR phase logic in detail:\n\n```js\nfunction startEnterElevator(agent, action) {\n  agent.enterPhase = 'reserve';\n}\nfunction processEnterElevator(agent, motionDt) {\n  const a = agent.currentAction;\n  if (agent.enterPhase === 'reserve') {\n     pressCall(agent.floor, agent.dir);   // re-press in case cleared\n     if (!elevator.isAcceptingAt(agent.floor, agent.dir)) return false;\n     const spot = elevator.reserveBoardingSpot(agent);\n     if (!spot) return false;\n     agent.spot = spot; agent.enterPhase = 'walkDoor';\n     return false;\n  }\n  if (agent.enterPhase === 'walkDoor') {\n     // walk in world space to door threshold at x=spot.x, z = car front edge\n     const target = new THREE.Vector3(spotWorld.x, floorY, WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH/2 ... )\n```\nHmm: the doors are on +Z face of shaft; the car interior spans z ∈ [-1.5, 1.5]. Door threshold world pos: (spot.x, agent.floor*FH, 1.4). Agent walks from its position to that point. Must ensure path isn't blocked by walls — it's inside the shaft opening region... The shaft walls: shaft is a column; front face at z=1.5 has doors. When doors open, agent steps in.\n\nThen when agent reaches threshold (z >= 1.3 say), reparent to car group and set local position = spot coords, phase 'walkSpot'. Then walk within car to spot (in car-local coordinates). Since collision skips car-parented agents ✓.\n\ncompleteBoard → action complete.\n\nFor EXIT_ELEVATOR: at start, registerDisembark(agent) (holds doors), then phase 'walkDoor' in car local space toward (spot.x, 0, 1.3); when reached, reparent to scene with world position preserved; then walk along path from elevWait? Spec: \"walk to elevWait on the target floor; completeDisembark\". So after exiting, set agent.path = [elevWaitPos] and walk there (in world space), then completeDisembark.\n\nCareful: when reparenting to car group, the person's local position must be spot coords with y=0 (feet). Person origin at feet ✓ so local y = 0 works if car floor is at group origin level. Car group origin at car floor level (y = pos*FH) → local y=0 for standing person ✓.\n\nBut note: the agent's group position while in scene is at world coords; when reparenting, do:\n```js\nconst worldPos = new THREE.Vector3(); agent.group.getWorldPosition(worldPos);\nagent.group.parent.remove(agent.group);\nelevator.carGroup.add(agent.group);\nconst local = elevator.carGroup.worldToLocal(worldPos.clone());\nagent.group.position.copy(local);\n```\n✓.\n\nAnd when leaving: capture world pos, remove from car, add to scene (or buildingGroup), set position = worldPos.\n\nNote agents' groups are added directly to `scene` for simplicity (so collision \"same parent\" check works: parent === scene or parent === elevator.carGroup). I'll add all agent groups to `scene` directly and reparent to carGroup when boarding ✓.\n\nNow, the y position while in car: local y = 0 → person feet at car floor ✓. But car floor mesh is at group origin? Let's build car floor box centered slightly below origin (y=-0.05) so feet sit on it ✓.\n\nNow `agent.floor` and standing y when in scene: agent.group.position.y = floorIndex * FLOOR_HEIGHT ✓ (person origin at feet).\n\nAlright, also need to handle agents walking on the sidewalk outside (floor 0, y=0) ✓.\n\nCollision skip for sitting agents ✓ and car agents ✓ and ENTER_ELEVATOR agents ✓.\n\nNow let me think about `applyCollisions` skipping agents that are DISABLED/GONE ✓.\n\nTime to write code. I'll write in a structured way. Let's start with person.js (short), then elevator_logic.js + tests, then world.js, elevator.js, sim.js, index.html.\n\nLet me write elevator_logic.js carefully.\n\n```js\n(function (root) {\n  const STATE = { IDLE:'IDLE', MOVING:'MOVING', DOOR_OPENING:'DOOR_OPENING', DOOR_OPEN:'DOOR_OPEN', DOOR_CLOSING:'DOOR_CLOSING' };\n\n  class ElevatorLogic {\n    constructor(opts) {\n      opts = opts || {};\n      this.floorCount = opts.floorCount !== undefined ? opts.floorCount : 6;\n      this.maxCapacity = ...4;\n      this.floorHeight = ...3.4;\n      this.minDoorOpenS = opts.minDoorOpenS ?? 2.5;\n      this.maxDoorOpenS = opts.maxDoorOpenS ?? 10;\n      this.doorTravelS = 0.8;\n      this.floorsPerSecond = 1.6;\n      this.spots = [ {index:0,x:-0.7,y:0,z:-0.5}, ... ];\n      this.reset();\n    }\n    reset() {...}\n    callUp(f), callDown(f), pressDestination(f)\n    isAcceptingAt(floor, direction)\n    currentCapacityFree()\n    reserveBoardingSpot(person)\n    completeBoard(person), registerDisembark(person), completeDisembark(person)\n    tick(dt)\n  }\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n```\n\ntick logic:\n```js\ntick(dt) {\n  if (this.state === STATE.MOVING) {\n     this.reevaluateTarget(); // scan for closer stop in same direction\n     if (this.targetFloor === null) { /* nothing? then stop & open doors at current floor */ }\n     const dir = Math.sign(this.targetFloor - this.currentFloor); ... move carPos toward target\n     if reached: this.currentFloor = target; state = DOOR_OPENING; doorTimer=0; servedThisDoorCycle=false; reopenedAtSameFloor=false; clear calls/destinations for that floor at arrival (per rules) — clearing happens on door open.\n  } else if DOOR_OPENING: timer += dt; if >= doorTravelS → state=DOOR_OPEN, doorOpenElapsed=0, serveFloor() (clear destinations/calls), \n  else if DOOR_OPEN: doorOpenElapsed += dt; if ((pending empty && elapsed>=min) || elapsed>=max) → DOOR_CLOSING\n  else if DOOR_CLOSING: timer+=dt; if >= travelS → pick target → MOVING or IDLE.\n  else IDLE: pick target → MOVING (if found).\n}\n```\n\nserveFloor at door open: \n- clear destinations for this floor\n- clear hall call for current direction\n- if no more stops in current direction, also clear opposite-direction call at this floor.\n\nHmm \"clear the served hall call for the current direction\" — but what about a call in the opposite direction at this floor? Keep it unless no work ahead (then clear & serve? Actually clearing means removing from set; but people waiting there need service... The spec says: \"At each door-open arrival, clear destinations for that floor and clear the served hall call for the current direction. If no more stops exist in the current direction, also clear the opposite-direction call at this floor so it can be served before leaving.\" Hmm — clearing a call means it's been registered/served? In our sim, agents re-press each frame while waiting, so clearing is fine (they'll re-press).\n\nCareful with test 4: moving up with work above; DOWN call at current or lower floor should not reverse until upward work served. Our pickTarget scans current direction first ✓. But serveFloor's \"if no more stops in current direction, clear opposite-direction call at this floor\" — that could remove a down call at the arrival floor... but then agents re-press. In test 4 we'd assert car reaches upper floors before reversing; if the up work exists, no clearing happens ✓.\n\npickTarget implementation:\n```js\npickTarget() {\n  const cur = this.currentFloor;\n  // passenger destinations outrank hall calls\n  if (this.destinations.size > 0) {\n    let best=null;\n    for (const f of this.destinations) {\n      if ((f - cur) * this.direction > 0) { pick nearest in direction }\n    }\n    if (best===null) pick nearest destination overall (direction inferred);\n    return best;\n  }\n  // hall calls, current direction first\n  const dir = this.direction;\n  let best=null;\n  if (dir !== 0) { for f in cur+dir..bounds step dir: if call matching dir → return f }\n  // reverse\n  for f in cur-dir .. bounds step -dir: if matching call → set direction=-dir, return f\n  // any call at current floor? guard against reopen loop\n  ...\n}\n```\nCareful with \"same floor cannot reopen indefinitely while destinations exist\" — but here destinations empty. Add `reopenCount` guard: allow same-floor target only if no other work anywhere and reopenedThisCycle is false.\n\nLet me define pickTarget to never return cur when called at door-close transition, unless it's the only active call AND !this.reopenedAtSameFloor (reset on leaving floor). Actually simpler: in DOOR_CLOSING→pick, skip current floor entirely; if nothing else found → IDLE (calls remain queued; agents re-press and... but who triggers a new trip? In sim, waiting agents keep pressing; when car is IDLE at floor 0 with an up call at floor 0, we should open doors again to let them board. So IDLE state should check: if there's a call at current floor → DOOR_OPENING (serve). That handles it, and the reopen guard prevents infinite loop only \"while destinations exist\".\n\nLet me define:\n- In IDLE: if any calls/destinations → pick target; if target === currentFloor → open doors to serve (that's fine, we're idle, not a loop). But add guard `reopenCountAtCurrentFloor` incremented each time we reopen at same floor without leaving; cap at 2 while destinations exist.\n\nHmm, tests: test 1 requires after door close with full car + destinations above → target > 0 ✓ (destinations branch wins). Test 2: passengers>0 and destinations non-empty, adding a same-floor hall call must not cause immediate reopen at same floor ✓ (pickTarget returns destination; also we never pick cur when other work exists).\n\nTest 3: repeatedly callUp(0) while riders have destinations → car still reaches a passenger destination ✓.\n\nTest 5: door hold & cap — need pending sets to keep doors open beyond min, then close at max even if pending non-empty ✓.\n\nTest 6: handshake test — simulate: pressDestination(5), board, etc., assert targetFloor eventually 5 and currentFloor reaches 5. I'll write a test that models the action sequence using logic API only.\n\nTest 7: reset clears everything including spotOccupancy (assert reserveBoardingSpot after reset returns index 0 and capacity full).\n\nNow writing tests requires knowing internal state names: `state`, `direction`, `currentFloor`, `targetFloor`, `upCalls`, `downCalls`, `destinations`, `passengers`, `pendingBoarders`, `pendingDisembark`. I'll expose those as public fields ✓.\n\nLet me now write all files. Start with person.js.\n\nI need to be careful about the static checker's handling of things like `this.spots` etc. Fine.\n\nOne more consideration: static checker flags unresolved refs; e.g., in sim.js referencing `THREE`, `window`, `document`, `requestAnimationFrame` — all known globals ✓. `module` known ✓ (in elevator_logic.js). `globalThis` known ✓.\n\nAlso careful: in world.js, using `performance.now()`? performance is known ✓.\n\nLet me write files now.\n\nFor HUD I'll create DOM elements; ensure no undefined refs.\n\nLet me draft sim.js structure fully before writing to avoid typos.\n\nsim.js outline:\n\n```js\nconst MAX_WORKERS = 20;\nconst MAX_VISITORS = 80;\nconst MAX_OCCUPANCY = MAX_WORKERS + MAX_VISITORS;\nlet targetOccupancy = 45;\nconst NAMES = [...];\n\nlet scene, camera, renderer, controls;\nlet world, elevator, clock;\nconst agents = [];\nconst seatReservations = new Set();\nlet hud = null;\n\nfunction randInt(a,b){...} function pickRandom(arr){...}\n\nfunction createClock() { return { simMinute: 7*60+30, timeScale:120, tick(realDt){...}, format(){...}, getDelta? } }\n```\nHmm spec says `realDt = min(0.05, clock.getDelta())`. So Clock has getDelta() returning real dt since last call. I'll implement clock with `_lastReal` using performance.now().\n\nClock.tick(realDt) advances simMinute; on wrap past 24*60 → newDay(): reset agents & elevator.\n\nLighting: `applyLighting(simHour)` uses keyframes and updates scene.background, sun light, ambient, hemi (store refs).\n\nAgents:\n```js\nfunction createAgents() { for i in 0..MAX_OCCUPANCY-1: role = i<MAX_WORKERS? WORKER : VISITOR; agent = {...}; }\n```\nDesk assignment: desks list from world floors (floors 1..5, each with 4 desks) → 20 desks. Assign worker i to desk i.\n\nAgent fields: id, name, role, group, floor, state, plan, currentActionIndex, hasLunched, arrivalTime, lunchTime, lunchDuration, departureTime, plannedMeetingTimes, homeFloor, deskId, deskWpName, deskDoorWpName, seatReservation (string key or null), path, pathIndex.\n\nLifecycle each frame:\n```js\nfunction updateAgent(agent, motionDt) {\n  if (agent.state === 'DISABLED' || agent.state === 'GONE') return;\n  if (agent.state === 'AWAY') { if simMinute >= arrivalTime && businessHours → spawn & set plan }\n  ... dispatch loop up to 16: run current action; if complete advance.\n}\n```\n\nAction processing function `processAction(agent, motionDt)` returns true when done.\n\nLet me write each action handler.\n\nWALK_TO_WP:\n```js\nfunction startWalk(agent, floor, wpName) {\n  const nodes = world.floors[floor].nodes;\n  const startName = nearestNodeName(nodes, agent.group.position); // must be on same floor\n  const path = bfsPath(nodes, startName, wpName);\n  agent.path = path; agent.pathIndex = 0; agent.walkFloor = floor;\n}\n```\nIf agent is currently inside car... shouldn't happen for WALK_TO_WP.\n\nprocess: move toward path[idx]; when within PERSON_R*0.6 (~0.25) → idx++; if idx>=len complete. Also set isWalking true, isSitting false during walk; y = floorY (unless sitting? no).\n\nStall detection per spec.\n\nWAIT_AT_PANEL:\n```js\nstartAction: store untilMin? no. Each frame: press call for dir at agent.floor; if elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && capacity free → complete. Also walk to panel position gently? The plan precedes with WALK_TO_WP(elevWait). I'll also nudge the agent toward elevWait node if far (>0.6).\n```\n\nSIT: snap to sit target pos + jitter for standing waypoints; set facing; isSitting true; y = floorY - 0.35 (or car? no, SIT only on floors). Complete immediately.\n\nSTAND: isSitting=false; y restore = agent.inCar ? car local 0 : floorY. Careful: STAND may be called while in car? Plans: at desk decision points they're at desk. Fine — handle both.\n\nHmm, when standing inside the car, group parent is carGroup and position.y should be spot.y (0). I'll handle: if parent === elevator.carGroup → keep local y = 0 else floorY - ... Let me implement `restoreAgentGround(agent)`.\n\nWAIT_SIM(minutes): startAction resolves untilMin = simMinute + minutes; process checks clock.simMinute >= untilMin.\n\nPICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY: calls chooseNextActivity(agent) which sets agent.plan and index=0, then the next action starts. Careful with dispatch loop recursion: PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY completes immediately and returns true; plan replaced.\n\nENTER_STATE(state): set agent.state = state; complete.\n\nEXIT_BUILDING: remove group from scene (from its parent), state GONE, release seat reservation.\n\nMARK_LUNCHED: hasLunched=true.\n\nRELEASE_SEAT: delete key.\n\nPRESS_FLOOR(floor): elevator.pressDestination(floor); complete.\n\nNow chooseNextActivity per spec order.\n\nPlan compilers as described. Visitor weights.\n\nLet me also handle \"visit a coworker\": pick random agent currently AT_DESK → walk to their office door node on that floor (may need elevator if different floor). Implement: if agent.floor !== targetFloor → ride elevator down/up.\n\nSimplify with helper `planTravelTo(floor, wpName)` producing elevator actions when needed.\n\nNow HUD DOM: create div with time, sliders, breakdown. Use input type=range for speed (log-spaced stops array) and occupancy.\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll produce files then run checkers/tests.\n\nFor log-spaced slider: `const SPEED_STOPS = [1,2,4,8,16,30,60,120,240,400,600];` slider index 0..10, default index for 120 → position.\n\nLet me write everything now. I'll be systematic and then test.\n\nRegarding runtime_check: it probes `index.html` in eval dir; runs static check + loads page via http server presumably. It checks canvas count, nonblank, animation frames, scene object count, dynamic changes. Our sim should produce motion ✓.\n\nLet me write person.js first.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Playwright is available and the workspace is empty. Let me build the files, starting with `person.js`.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"2WqWufkOX9NrQOZRVhpTOUmejlKItKEb","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/person.js","content":"// person.js - person mesh factory + walk/sit animation (classic browser script, no ES modules)\n\nconst PERSON_SHIRT_COLORS = [\n    0x4a7bd6, 0xd9534f, 0x3f9c6d, 0xb8863b, 0x7a5cc8,\n    0x2f7f8f, 0xc25b80, 0x5a6f8a, 0xa4463d, 0x4c9a2f\n];\n\nconst PERSON_SKIN_COLORS = [\n    0xf1c9a0, 0xe8b98a, 0xd29b72, 0xb5764f, 0x8c5a3b, 0xf7dcb8\n];\n\nconst PERSON_LEG_COLORS = [\n    0x2f3b4c, 0x3d4a5c, 0x4a4038, 0x5b5f6b, 0x334152, 0x6b4a3a\n];\n\nfunction paletteColor(palette) {\n    return palette[Math.floor(Math.random() * palette.length)];\n}\n\nconst PERSON_HIP_Y = 0.82;\nconst PERSON_LEG_LEN = 0.80;\nconst PERSON_SHOULDER_Y = 1.44;\nconst PERSON_ARM_LEN = 0.60;\nconst PERSON_HEAD_Y = 1.63;\n\nfunction buildLimb(pivotGroup, length, radius, material) {\n    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius, radius * 0.85, length, 8), material);\n    mesh.position.y = -length / 2;\n    pivotGroup.add(mesh);\n}\n\nfunction createPerson(opts) {\n    const options = opts || {};\n    const shirtColor = options.bodyColor !== undefined ? options.bodyColor : paletteColor(PERSON_SHIRT_COLORS);\n    const skinColor = options.skinColor !== undefined ? options.skinColor : paletteColor(PERSON_SKIN_COLORS);\n    const legColor = options.legColor !== undefined ? options.legColor : paletteColor(PERSON_LEG_COLORS);\n\n    const shirtMat = new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: shirtColor });\n    const skinMat = new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: skinColor });\n    const legMat = new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: legColor });\n\n    const group = new THREE.Group();\n\n    // Legs: each leg is its own group pivoting at the hip, cylinder hanging below.\n    const legLeft = new THREE.Group();\n    legLeft.position.set(-0.14, PERSON_HIP_Y, 0);\n    buildLimb(legLeft, PERSON_LEG_LEN, 0.10, legMat);\n    group.add(legLeft);\n\n    const legRight = new THREE.Group();\n    legRight.position.set(0.14, PERSON_HIP_Y, 0);\n    buildLimb(legRight, PERSON_LEG_LEN, 0.10, legMat);\n    group.add(legRight);\n\n    // Torso\n    const torso = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.22, 0.24, PERSON_SHOULDER_Y - PERSON_HIP_Y, 10), shirtMat);\n    torso.position.y = (PERSON_HIP_Y + PERSON_SHOULDER_Y) / 2;\n    group.add(torso);\n\n    // Head\n    const head = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.17, 12, 10), skinMat);\n    head.position.y = PERSON_HEAD_Y;\n    group.add(head);\n\n    // Small hemisphere nose on the +Z face of the head so facing reads top-down.\n    const nose = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.055, 8, 6, 0, Math.PI), skinMat);\n    nose.position.set(0, PERSON_HEAD_Y - 0.02, 0.17);\n    group.add(nose);\n\n    // Arms pivot at the shoulder.\n    const armLeft = new THREE.Group();\n    armLeft.position.set(-0.30, PERSON_SHOULDER_Y, 0);\n    buildLimb(armLeft, PERSON_ARM_LEN, 0.075, shirtMat);\n    group.add(armLeft);\n\n    const armRight = new THREE.Group();\n    armRight.position.set(0.30, PERSON_SHOULDER_Y, 0);\n    buildLimb(armRight, PERSON_ARM_LEN, 0.075, shirtMat);\n    group.add(armRight);\n\n    // Feet marker so the origin sits at the feet (local y = 0).\n    const feet = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.36, 0.04, 0.28), legMat);\n    feet.position.y = 0.02;\n    group.add(feet);\n\n    group.userData = {\n        isWalking: false,\n        isSitting: false,\n        walkPhase: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\n        legLeft: legLeft,\n        legRight: legRight,\n        armLeft: armLeft,\n        armRight: armRight,\n        shirtColor: shirtColor\n    };\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nfunction animatePersonWalking(person, dt) {\n    const data = person.userData;\n    if (!data || !data.legLeft) return;\n\n    if (data.isSitting) {\n        data.walkPhase = 0;\n        data.legLeft.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n        data.legRight.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n        data.armLeft.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 4;\n        data.armRight.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 4;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    if (data.isWalking) {\n        data.walkPhase += dt * 8;\n        const swing = Math.sin(data.walkPhase);\n        data.legLeft.rotation.x = swing * 0.6;\n        data.legRight.rotation.x = -swing * 0.6;\n        data.armLeft.rotation.x = -swing * 0.5;\n        data.armRight.rotation.x = swing * 0.5;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    data.walkPhase = 0;\n    data.legLeft.rotation.x = 0;\n    data.legRight.rotation.x = 0;\n    data.armLeft.rotation.x = 0;\n    data.armRight.rotation.x = 0;\n}\n\nwindow.createPerson = createPerson;\nwindow.animatePersonWalking = animatePersonWalking;\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"lmstudio","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-gsq-rco","usage":{"input":24593,"output":19942,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18323,"totalTokens":44535,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791652102157,"responseId":"chatcmpl-qr041eau12m5kv6vvea2i8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":3727351,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"2WqWufkOX9NrQOZRVhpTOUmejlKItKEb","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/person.js"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1791655829517},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now elevator_logic.js.\n\nCareful design of the state machine and pickTarget. Let me write it.\n\nConstants inside: MIN_DOOR_OPEN_S = 2.5, MAX_DOOR_OPEN_S = 10, DOOR_TRAVEL_S = 0.8, FLOOR_TRAVEL... speed floors per second = 1.6.\n\nState machine tick(dt).\n\nAlso need `carPos` continuous for visual adapter: `this.carPosition` in floor units (float). Use `this.carFloorPos`.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```js\n(function (root) {\n    const STATES = ['IDLE','MOVING','DOOR_OPENING','DOOR