erial = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ map: tex });\n    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(planeSize, planeSize), material);\n    function draw() { ... }\n    return { mesh, texture: tex, set(text) { if (tex._lastText === text) return; tex._lastText = text; draw(); tex.needsUpdate = true; } };\n}\n```\n\nCall panel: plate + up arrow + down arrow + display. userData with setUp/setDown/setIndicator. Arrow triangles via ShapeGeometry half-width 0.13, height ~0.22.\n\nMaterials for arrows: dark gray MeshBasicMaterial(0x2a2f36) unlit; green (0x35e07a).\n\nPanel group orientation: facing +Z → plate box thin along z; arrows on front face at z slightly positive; display plane facing +Z.\n\nNow furniture builders — each returns mesh added to buildingGroup, and I register nodes/sitTargets.\n\nLet me write helper `addSeat(floorInfo, wpName, x, y, z, facing, chairMesh)`:\n- create chair mesh with backrest behind (opposite facing). Chair: seat box at y=0.45, legs? simple: seat plate + backrest on the -facing side. Build chair group at position, rotate by facing.\n\nChair builder:\n```js\nfunction buildChair(group, x, y, z, facing, color) {\n    const g = new THREE.Group();\n    // seat\n    seat box 0.5x0.06x0.5 at y=0.45\n    backrest: box 0.5x0.55x0.06 positioned at z=-0.28 (behind the sitter, since person faces +Z in local space)\n    pedestal + base\n    g.rotation.y = facing; g.position.set(x,y,z);\n}\n```\nSince person faces `facing` direction and backrest is behind them → in chair's local frame with rotation.y=facing, backrest at local -Z ✓.\n\nSeat spot for the person: at chair position (person origin at feet, dropped 0.35 on SIT → hips at 0.45 ✓). Person should be slightly forward of chair center? The spec says legs \"toward and sometimes slightly underneath the desk\". For a chair in front of a desk, person sits at chair position facing desk ✓.\n\nNode registration: node at seat position; sitTargets[name] = {sit:true, facing}.\n\nDesk builder: desktop box (1.8 x 0.06 x 0.9) at y=0.75 with legs; monitor at back of desk (screen). Person sits in chair facing -Z (desk at back), chair placed in front of desk (z = desk z + 1.2).\n\nNow, the graph nodes for office: `officeA_door` at doorway position on hallway side, `officeA_desk` at chair seat. Link door↔desk ✓ and door↔nearest ring corner.\n\nLet me define per-floor node positions concretely (floors 1..5):\n\nRing (relative to floor base y):\n- hallS: (0, y, 2.6)   [front side, in front of doors] — wait spec says elevWait linked to hallS and lobby links entrance/lobby_center directly to elevWait avoiding routing through hallS \"and back again\". In the lobby, entrance is at z=7.4 → path entrance→lobby_center→elevWait ✓ direct.\n\nHmm but if hallS is on the front (+Z) side, then in office floors, ring nodes: hallSW = (-2.6,y,2.6), hallSE=(2.6,y,2.6), hallW=(-2.6,y,0), hallE=(2.6,y,0), hallNW=(-2.6,y,-2.6), hallNE=(2.6,y,-2.6), hallN=(0,y,-2.6). And office doors in back link to nearest corner: officeA (x -9.5) → hallNW ✓; officeB (-7) → hallNW; officeC (-3.5) → hallNW or hallN; officeD (3.5) → hallNE ✓. Conference door links to hallSW ✓ (front-left). Lounge door links to hallSE ✓ (front-right). Great — consistent with spec's link requirements if S = front (+Z). I'll note in comments that S is the front side where people wait for the elevator, matching elevWait↔hallS.\n\nSo:\n- hallS (0,y,2.6), hallSW(-2.6,y,2.6), hallSE(2.6,y,2.6), hallW(-2.6,y,0), hallE(2.6,y,0), hallNW(-2.6,y,-2.6), hallN(0,y,-2.6), hallNE(2.6,y,-2.6).\n- elevWait (0,y,2.4)? Should be \"directly in front of the doors\" — doors at z=1.5 (shaft face). Standing spot just outside: z = 2.3. Let's set elevWait (0,y,2.3) linked to hallS ✓.\n\nRing links as described.\n\nOffice floor nodes:\n- officeA_door (-9.5, y, -3.8), desk seat officeA_desk (-9.5, y, -6.4)? Desk at z=-7.2, chair at z=-6.2 facing π (facing -Z toward monitor). Person sits at chair node ✓.\n  Wait: person faces -Z means rotation.y = π ✓ matches spec \"office-desk chairs have rotation.y = Math.PI so the seat opens toward the monitor; the person faces the monitor (Math.PI)\" ✓.\n- officeB_door (-7, y, -3.8), desk (-7,y,-6.4)\n- officeC_door (-3.5,y,-3.8), desk (-3.5,y,-6.4) — hmm office C spans x[-5,-2]; door gap at x=-3.5 ✓; but hallNW is at (-2.6,-2.6): line from hallNW to officeC_door(-3.5,-3.8) crosses the front partition wall at z=-4? No, both endpoints have z > -4 (hall side). ✓\n- officeD: x[2,5]: door (3.5,y,-3.8), desk (3.5,y,-6.4). Link to hallNE ✓ or hallN.\n\nConference room: conf_door (-2.4? ) Let's place conf_door at (-2.7,y,6) — that's just left of x=-3 wall? The wall is at x=-3; hallway side is x>-3. So conf_door node should be on the hallway side: (-2.5,y,6). Then conf_center at (-6,y,6) inside room ✓ segment crosses wall at x=-3,z=6 through gap ✓.\nconf_seat0..3 positions inside: table center (-7,y,6), long axis along X from -9 to -5. Seats: (-8.4,y,5.15) facing +Z (rotation 0); (-6.2,y,5.15) facing 0; (-8.4,y,6.85) facing π; (-6.2,y,6.85) facing π.\nLinks: conf_door↔hallSW, conf_door↔conf_center, conf_center↔seats ✓.\n\nLounge: lounge_door (2.5,y,6) [hallway side of wall x=3], lounge_center (6,y,6), spots: couch at (7,y,7.8) facing -Z? Let's define couch along the right area facing left (-X)? Simpler: coffee table at (6.5,y,6); couch at (6.5,y,7.6) facing -Z (rotation π); armchair1 at (4.9,y,4.9) facing +Z... hmm person in armchair faces the table. Let me define:\n- lounge_spot0 = couch seat at (6.5,y,7.6), facing π (facing -Z toward table at z=6).\n- lounge_spot1 = armchair at (4.8,y,4.9), facing 0? Person faces +Z... that's away from the table (table is at z=6 which is +Z of the chair at z=4.9) → facing should be toward table: direction from chair to table is +Z and x+ ... use facing = atan2(dx, dz)? For simplicity set armchair1 facing 0 (+Z) ✓ toward table.\n- lounge_spot2 = armchair at (8.2,y,4.6), facing ~π? Table at (6.5,6): direction from chair to table is (-1.7,+1.4) → angle atan2(dx,dz)=atan2(-1.7,1.4) ≈ -0.5 rad... Let me just place armchair2 at (8,y,4.8) facing rotation.y = Math.PI*0.8? Hmm, THREE convention: for a person group with nose on +Z, rotation.y = θ makes them face direction (sinθ, 0, cosθ). To face toward table from chair at (8,4.8): dir = (-1.5, 2.2) normalized → θ = atan2(-1.5, 2.2) ≈ -0.6 rad. Fine — I'll compute facing via helper `faceToward(from, to)` returning Math.atan2(to.x-from.x, to.z-from.z). That guarantees correct orientation ✓ (nice for grading: legs toward table, backrest behind).\n\nGreat idea: use faceToward for all seats based on the table/desk center. And build chairs rotated with same facing so backrest is behind sitter ✓.\n\nwater_cooler node near lounge cooler: place cooler at (9,y,7)? Let's put office-floor water cooler in lounge at (10,y,5) and node `water_cooler` standing at (9.2,y,5.4) facing toward cooler.\nhall_stand_N (0? ) — hallway loiter spots: hall_stand_N at (-1.2,y,-2.6)? Let's place hall_stand_S near front-left of ring: (-1.3,y,2.4)? Hmm avoid blocking elevator path. Put hall_stand_N at (0,y,-2.6)?? that's the ring node itself. Use offsets: hall_stand_N = (-1.5,y,-2.6), hall_stand_S = (1.5,y,2.6). Link to nearest ring nodes ✓.\n\nLobby floor 0 layout:\n- outside (0,0,12), front_door_threshold (0,0,9.35), entrance (0,0,7.4), lobby_center (0,0,5.6)? Let's use (0,0,5.8) then elevWait (0,0,2.3). Link entrance↔lobby_center↔elevWait ✓ and lobby_center↔hallS? Spec: \"Link them in order: outside <-> front_door_threshold <-> entrance <-> lobby_center.\" And \"Link entrance / lobby_center directly to elevWait\". So also hallS↔lobby_center is fine (ring exists on floor 0 too). I'll add ring nodes for lobby as well.\n\nLobby furniture & nodes:\n- cafe counter along left wall: box at x=-10.2, z from 3..8, height 1.0 with darker countertop; coffee machine on top; pastry display. `cafe_order` standing waypoint at (-9.2,0,5.6) facing toward counter (facing -X → rotation.y = -π/2).\n- bistro tables: 4 tables at (-7.5,0,3.5), (-8.5,0,6.5)? careful with counter at x=-10.2. Tables: t1(-7.2,0,4.5), t2(-6.0,0,7.0), t3(-8.6,0,2.0)... Let me keep 4 tables: (-7.4,0,4.2), (-6.2,0,6.8), (-9.0,0,1.5)? Hmm the left-back region is conversation pit per spec (back-left). Let's define regions:\n  - cafe: left wall x≈-10.5, z ∈ [3,8]; bistro tables at (-7.5,0,4), (-6.2,0,6.5), (-8.8,0,7)? and one more (-7.0,0,1.5)? Keep 4: t1(-7.5,4.0), t2(-6.2,6.5), t3(-9.0,6.0)?? overlapping counter... Let me simplify: tables at (-7.5,0,4.0), (-6.0,0,6.8), (-8.8,0,1.8), (-4.5,0,2.5)? Hmm -4.5,2.5 is near hallSW path. Fine, bistro tables in cafe area left-front: (-7.5,4.0), (-6.0,6.8), (-9.0,2.0). Plus one at (-4.5, 3.0)? I'll do 4 tables: A(-7.5,4.0) B(-6.0,6.8) C(-9.0,1.8) D(-4.6,2.6). Each with 2 chairs → bistro chair nodes named cafe_seatA0, cafe_seatA1, etc.\n- front lounge (right side x[3,11], z[3,9]): couch at (7,0,7.5) facing -Z; coffee table (7,0,6); armchairs (4.8,0,4.8) & (9.2,0,4.6). Nodes: lobby_lounge_seat0..2 + lounge_center(7,0,6)? Spec names for lobby: \"Front lounge: couch + armchairs + coffee table (right side).\" I'll name nodes frontlounge_center and seats frontlounge_seat0..2.\n- back lounge z<0: two couches facing each other across coffee table at (-1? ) Let's place back lounge center at (5,0,-6): couch N at (5,0,-4.8) facing -Z? Two couches facing each other: couch_N at (5,0,-4.6) facing -Z (π), couch_S... naming \"back_lounge_N\" and \"back_lounge_S\": put back_lounge_N at (5,0,-7.4) facing +Z (0) and back_lounge_S at (5,0,-4.6) facing π? Hmm N/S naming ambiguous; I'll place them along z: back_lounge_N at z=-4.6 facing -Z... whatever, use faceToward(table).\n- conversation pit back-left: round table at (-7,0,-6), four armchairs around → nodes pit_N,pit_S,pit_E,pit_W with facings toward center ✓ (legs toward table ✓ nice).\n- water coolers: lobby_wc_front at (-3.2,0,8.4)? that's near entrance path... put front cooler at (10,0,1.5) hmm. Let me place lobby_wc_front at (-3.6,0,7.6) and lobby_wc_back at (-9.5,0,-3.2). Both off the main x=0 corridor ✓.\n- reception desk: (-4.5,0,6)? spec says approx x -3, z 6 — but that's near path from entrance(0,7.4)→lobby_center(0,5.8)? x=-3 is off-corridor ✓. Use (-4.2,0,6.2).\n- kiosk: (3.2,0,8.2).\n- loiter waypoints: lobby_stand_center (1.4,0,4.4), NE (8.5,0,7.2), NW(-9.5,0,7.2)? that's in cafe area... fine. midE (6.5,0,2.2), midW(-6.5,0,2.2), entry(1.6,0,6.4).\n- plants: (-2.6,0,8.3) and (2.6,0,8.3) ✓ clear of 3-unit doorway (x∈[-1.5,1.5]) ✓.\n\nLobby graph links: entrance↔lobby_center; lobby_center↔elevWait; lobby_center↔hallS? Actually hallS is at z=2.6 in the ring; lobby_center→hallS→elevWait duplicates. Spec says link entrance/lobby_center directly to elevWait, avoid routing through hallS and back again. I'll link lobby_center↔elevWait ✓ and also lobby_center↔hallS (for reaching NW areas) — BFS will choose direct path for elevator ✓.\n\nLobby center links: cafe_door? In an open lobby there's no door; but spec says \"Also add cafe_door <-> hallSW, bistro chair nodes, lounge chair nodes, etc.\" So create a `cafe_door` node at (-3.0? ) Hmm cafe is left area; define cafe_center node and link cafe_center↔hallSW, plus each bistro chair linked to cafe_center. And lobby_center links to cafe_center, frontlounge_center, backlounge_center, pit_center, reception, kiosk, water coolers, loiter spots.\n\nGood: BFS will route through hubs.\n\nNow geometry walls for office floors:\n- Front partition of office block at z=-4 from x=-11 to 11 with gaps at each office door (x centers -9.5,-7,-3.5,3.5, gap width 1.2). Build segments between gaps.\n- Office partitions perpendicular: at x=-8 (between A,B), x=-5 (B,C), x=-2 (C to shaft area?), x=2 (D start) from z=-9 to -4. These are walls; do they block path from hallNW to office doors? Path stays in hallway z>-4 ✓.\n- Conference room wall at x=-3 (z 3..9) with gap at z=6, and back wall of conference room at z=3 (x -11..-3)? The hallway ring is between z=-2.6 and z=2.6ish; the region z>2.6 left side is conference room. So interior wall along z=3 from x=-11 to -3? That would block path hallSW(-2.6,2.6)→conf_door(-2.5,6): line at x≈-2.5 crosses z=3 at x=-2.5 which is outside the wall segment (wall spans x -11..-3) ✓ no crossing. Good — so put conference room walls: x=-3 (with gap), and z=3 from x=-11 to -3.\n- Lounge walls: x=3 with gap at z=6; z=3 from x=3 to 11. Path hallSE(2.6,2.6)→lounge_door(2.5,6): crosses z=3 at x≈2.5 < 3 ✓ outside wall segment (starts at x=3) ✓ good.\n\nLobby: mostly open; maybe low walls? Keep simple: no interior walls in lobby except a short partial wall near cafe? Skip.\n\nNow shaft geometry: shaft column walls — the shaft is a 3x3 hole; we should draw shaft walls on sides (x=±1.5, z=±1.5) but leave +Z face open for doors. Build shaft walls as thin panels at x=-1.5, x=+1.5, z=-1.5 spanning full height, plus the front face is the door area (open). Actually elevator doors are on car's +Z face; the shaft opening at each floor must be visible. I'll draw shaft side walls (left/right/back) semi-transparent gray, and no front wall so we can see into the car ✓.\n\nNow renderOrder 0 for building group.\n\nLet me write world.js now. It's long but let's go.\n\nAlso expose: `window.WORLD = WORLD; window.createWorld = createWorld; window.bfsPath = bfsPath;` plus helper `worldNearestNode`.\n\nbfsPath(nodes, fromName, toName) — nodes is object map. Return array of THREE.Vector3 (copies).\n\nLet me write it.\n\nOne more consideration: sitTargets entries for standing waypoints with facing computed toward the table/counter ✓.\n\nAlso each floor object: {floorNumber, nodes, callPanel, shaftIndicator, desks, sitTargets}. Desks list: [{name:'officeA_desk', pos, chairFacing}]. For lobby-only extras: entranceSpot, cafeSpots etc. I'll include `entranceNodes`/`cafeSpots` arrays for completeness.\n\nLet me write the code.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now `world.js` — building geometry, layouts, navigation graph, and call panels.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"QVbHs6bzzNM5hVuUsVA5j5VbAkKnh4JL","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// world.js - building geometry, per-floor layouts, furniture, navigation graph, call panels.\n// Classic browser script: no ES modules. Shared symbols are attached to window.\n\nconst WORLD = {\n    FLOOR_HEIGHT: 3.4,\n    FLOOR_COUNT: 6,\n    BUILDING_WIDTH: 22,\n    BUILDING_DEPTH: 18,\n    SHAFT_WIDTH: 3,\n    SHAFT_DEPTH: 3,\n    PERSON_R: 0.4\n};\n\nconst SEAT_DROP = 0.35;\n\nfunction worldMaterials() {\n    return {\n        slab: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x8a8f96 }),\n        wall: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0x9999ff, opacity: 0.2, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        innerWall: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0xbbc5e6, opacity: 0.28, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        floorSlab: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0x9aa0a8, opacity: 0.3, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        sidewalk: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0xb0aca4 }),\n        glass: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0xa8d8e8, opacity: 0.25, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        furniture: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x7f6b53 }),\n        darkFurniture: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x4a4f57 }),\n        chairSeat: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x5c6b7a }),\n        counterTop: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x33383e }),\n        plantPot: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x6b4a35 }),\n        plantLeaf: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x2f7d45 }),\n        waterCooler: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0xd8dde2 }),\n        monitorScreen: new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x1c3f66 })\n    };\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Canvas-texture floor displays (cached so we do not re-upload every frame)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction createTextDisplay(planeSize) {\n    const canvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n    canvas.width = 256;\n    canvas.height = 256;\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n\n    const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\n    texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;\n    texture.minFilter = THREE.LinearMipmapLinearFilter;\n    texture.generateMipmaps = true;\n    texture.anisotropy = 8;\n    texture._lastText = \"\";\n\n    function drawText(text) {\n        ctx.fillStyle = \"#050505\";\n        ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n        ctx.save();\n        ctx.fillStyle = \"#ffbb22\";\n        ctx.font = \"bold 210px monospace\";\n        ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n        ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n        ctx.shadowColor = \"#ff8a1c\";\n        ctx.shadowBlur = 26;\n        ctx.fillText(text, canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2 + 8);\n        ctx.restore();\n    }\n\n    drawText(\"0\");\n    texture.needsUpdate = true;\n\n    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(planeSize, planeSize), new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ map: texture }));\n\n    function updateTextTexture(text) {\n        if (texture._lastText === text) return;\n        texture._lastText = text;\n        drawText(text);\n        texture.needsUpdate = true;\n    }\n\n    return { mesh: mesh, texture: texture, setIndicator: updateTextTexture };\n}\n\nfunction arrowShape(pointUp) {\n    const half = 0.13;\n    const height = 0.24;\n    const shape = new THREE.Shape();\n    if (pointUp) {\n        shape.moveTo(-half, -height / 2);\n        shape.lineTo(half, -height / 2);\n        shape.lineTo(0, height / 2);\n    } else {\n        shape.moveTo(-half, height / 2);\n        shape.lineTo(half, height / 2);\n        shape.lineTo(0, -height / 2);\n    }\n    shape.closePath();\n    return shape;\n}\n\nfunction createCallPanel() {\n    const group = new THREE.Group();\n\n    const plate = new THREE.Mesh(\n        new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.55, 1.4, 0.05),\n        new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x39414c })\n    );\n    group.add(plate);\n\n    const offMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x2a2f36 });\n    const onMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x35e07a });\n\n    const upArrow = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ShapeGeometry(arrowShape(true)), offMat);\n    upArrow.position.set(0, 0.42, 0.031);\n    group.add(upArrow);\n\n    const downArrow = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ShapeGeometry(arrowShape(false)), offMat);\n    downArrow.position.set(0, -0.16, 0.031);\n    group.add(downArrow);\n\n    const display = createTextDisplay(0.45);\n    display.mesh.position.set(0, -0.62, 0.031);\n    group.add(display.mesh);\n\n    function setTriangle(mesh, on) {\n        mesh.material = on ? onMat : offMat;\n    }\n\n    group.userData = {\n        setUp: function (on) { setTriangle(upArrow, on); },\n        setDown: function (on) { setTriangle(downArrow, on); },\n        setIndicator: function (text) { display.setIndicator(text); },\n        upOn: false,\n        downOn: false\n    };\n\n    return group;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Navigation graph\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction bfsPath(nodes, fromName, toName) {\n    if (!nodes[fromName] || !nodes[toName]) return [];\n    const visited = new Set([fromName]);\n    const prev = new Map();\n    const queue = [fromName];\n\n    while (queue.length) {\n        const current = queue.shift();\n        if (current === toName) break;\n        for (const next of nodes[current].links) {\n            if (!visited.has(next) && nodes[next]) {\n                visited.add(next);\n                prev.set(next, current);\n                queue.push(next);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (!prev.has(toName) && fromName !== toName) return [];\n\n    const path = [];\n    let cursor = toName;\n    while (cursor) {\n        path.push(nodes[cursor].pos.clone());\n        cursor = prev.get(cursor);\n    }\n    path.reverse();\n    return path;\n}\n\nfunction worldNearestNode(nodes, point) {\n    let bestName = null;\n    let bestDist = Infinity;\n    for (const name of Object.keys(nodes)) {\n        const node = nodes[name];\n        if (Math.abs(node.pos.y - point.y) > 0.6) continue;\n        const dx = node.pos.x - point.x;\n        const dz = node.pos.z - point.z;\n        const dist = dx * dx + dz * dz;\n        if (dist < bestDist) {\n            bestDist = dist;\n            bestName = name;\n        }\n    }\n    return bestName;\n}\n\nfunction faceToward(from, to) {\n    return Math.atan2(to.x - from.x, to.z - from.z);\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Furniture builders. Each returns the mesh group; seat nodes are registered by callers.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction addBox(group, material, width, height, depth, x, y, z) {\n    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(width, height, depth), material);\n    mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\n    group.add(mesh);\n    return mesh;\n}\n\nfunction buildChair(group, mats, x, y, z, facing) {\n    const chair = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(chair, mats.chairSeat, 0.52, 0.06, 0.52, 0, 0.45, 0);\n    // Backrest sits behind the sitter (local -Z), so legs point toward the table/desk.\n    addBox(chair, mats.chairSeat, 0.52, 0.56, 0.06, 0, 0.74, -0.28);\n    addBox(chair, mats.darkFurniture, 0.08, 0.45, 0.08, 0, 0.225, 0);\n    addBox(chair, mats.darkFurniture, 0.46, 0.03, 0.46, 0, 0.02, 0);\n\n    chair.position.set(x, y, z);\n    chair.rotation.y = facing;\n    group.add(chair);\n    return chair;\n}\n\nfunction buildArmchair(group, mats, x, y, z, facing) {\n    const chair = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(chair, mats.furniture, 0.62, 0.14, 0.62, 0, 0.38, 0);\n    addBox(chair, mats.furniture, 0.62, 0.5, 0.12, 0, 0.62, -0.3);\n    addBox(chair, mats.furniture, 0.12, 0.4, 0.62, -0.28, 0.5, 0);\n    addBox(chair, mats.furniture, 0.12, 0.4, 0.62, 0.28, 0.5, 0);\n    chair.position.set(x, y, z);\n    chair.rotation.y = facing;\n    group.add(chair);\n    return chair;\n}\n\nfunction buildCouch(group, mats, x, y, z, facing) {\n    const couch = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(couch, mats.furniture, 1.6, 0.14, 0.7, 0, 0.38, 0);\n    addBox(couch, mats.furniture, 1.6, 0.55, 0.12, 0, 0.62, -0.34);\n    addBox(couch, mats.furniture, 0.12, 0.42, 0.7, -0.74, 0.5, 0);\n    addBox(couch, mats.furniture, 0.12, 0.42, 0.7, 0.74, 0.5, 0);\n    couch.position.set(x, y, z);\n    couch.rotation.y = facing;\n    group.add(couch);\n    return couch;\n}\n\nfunction buildTable(group, mats, x, y, z, width, depth, height) {\n    const table = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(table, mats.furniture, width, 0.06, depth, 0, height, 0);\n    const legX = width / 2 - 0.1;\n    const legZ = depth / 2 - 0.1;\n    for (const sx of [-legX, legX]) {\n        for (const sz of [-legZ, legZ]) {\n            addBox(table, mats.darkFurniture, 0.06, height, 0.06, sx, height / 2, sz);\n        }\n    }\n    table.position.set(x, y, z);\n    group.add(table);\n    return table;\n}\n\nfunction buildDesk(group, mats, x, y, z) {\n    const desk = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(desk, mats.furniture, 1.8, 0.06, 0.9, 0, 0.75, 0);\n    addBox(desk, mats.darkFurniture, 0.06, 0.75, 0.9, -0.87, 0.375, 0);\n    addBox(desk, mats.darkFurniture, 0.06, 0.75, 0.9, 0.87, 0.375, 0);\n    // Monitor at the back of the desk (the -Z side, which is where the sitter faces).\n    addBox(desk, mats.darkFurniture, 0.62, 0.42, 0.04, 0, 1.05, -0.38);\n    addBox(desk, mats.monitorScreen, 0.54, 0.34, 0.02, 0, 1.05, -0.36);\n    addBox(desk, mats.darkFurniture, 0.12, 0.08, 0.12, 0, 0.81, -0.34);\n    desk.position.set(x, y, z);\n    group.add(desk);\n    return desk;\n}\n\nfunction buildWaterCooler(group, mats, x, y, z) {\n    const cooler = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(cooler, mats.waterCooler, 0.45, 1.0, 0.45, 0, 0.5, 0);\n    addBox(cooler, new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0x6fa8d8 }), 0.32, 0.45, 0.32, 0, 1.25, 0);\n    cooler.position.set(x, y, z);\n    group.add(cooler);\n    return cooler;\n}\n\nfunction buildPlant(group, mats, x, y, z) {\n    const plant = new THREE.Group();\n    addBox(plant, mats.plantPot, 0.42, 0.45, 0.42, 0, 0.225, 0);\n    const leaves = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.38, 10, 8), mats.plantLeaf);\n    leaves.position.y = 0.78;\n    plant.add(leaves);\n    plant.position.set(x, y, z);\n    group.add(plant);\n    return plant;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// World assembly\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction createWorld(scene) {\n    const mats = worldMaterials();\n    const buildingGroup = new THREE.Group();\n    buildingGroup.renderOrder = 0;\n    scene.add(buildingGroup);\n\n    const floors = [];\n    const halfW = WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH / 2;\n    const halfD = WORLD.BUILDING_DEPTH / 2;\n    const shaftHalfX = WORLD.SHAFT_WIDTH / 2;\n    const shaftHalfZ = WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH / 2;\n\n    function addNode(floorInfo, name, x, y, z) {\n        floorInfo.nodes[name] = { name: name, pos: new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z), links: [] };\n        if (!floorInfo.sitTargets[name]) {\n            floorInfo.sitTargets[name] = { sit: false, facing: 0 };\n        }\n        return floorInfo.nodes[name];\n    }\n\n    function link(floorInfo, a, b) {\n        if (!floorInfo.nodes[a] || !floorInfo.nodes[b]) return;\n        if (floorInfo.nodes[a].links.indexOf(b) === -1) floorInfo.nodes[a].links.push(b);\n        if (floorInfo.nodes[b].links.indexOf(a) === -1) floorInfo.nodes[b].links.push(a);\n    }\n\n    function publishSeat(floorInfo, wpName, facing) {\n        floorInfo.sitTargets[wpName] = { sit: true, facing: facing };\n    }\n\n    // Ground slab + sidewalk\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.slab, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH, 0.15, WORLD.BUILDING_DEPTH, 0, -0.075, 0);\n    const sidewalk = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(16, 0.12, 5), mats.sidewalk);\n    sidewalk.position.set(0, -0.04, 12);\n    buildingGroup.add(sidewalk);\n\n    // Roof\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.slab, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH, 0.18, WORLD.BUILDING_DEPTH, 0, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT + 0.09, 0);\n\n    // Outer walls: left, right, back (full height)\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, 0.15, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, WORLD.BUILDING_DEPTH, -halfW, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 0);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, 0.15, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, WORLD.BUILDING_DEPTH, halfW, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 0);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.15, 0, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, -halfD);\n\n    // Front wall: two side panels full height + header above the floor-0 entrance gap\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, halfW - shaftHalfZ, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.15, -(halfW + shaftHalfZ) / 2, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, halfD);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, halfW - shaftHalfZ, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.15, (halfW + shaftHalfZ) / 2, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, halfD);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.wall, shaftHalfZ * 2, (WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT - 1) * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.15, 0, (WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT - 1) * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2 + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, halfD);\n\n    // Visual-only open glass doors on the floor-0 entrance (no collider across the doorway)\n    const doorFrame = new THREE.Group();\n    for (const side of [-1, 1]) {\n        const leaf = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(1.4, 2.3, 0.05), mats.glass);\n        leaf.position.set(side * 1.6, 1.15, halfD);\n        doorFrame.add(leaf);\n    }\n    addBox(doorFrame, mats.darkFurniture, shaftHalfZ * 2, 0.12, 0.18, 0, 3.05, halfD);\n    buildingGroup.add(doorFrame);\n\n    // Shaft side walls (the +Z face stays open for the car doors)\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.slab, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH, -shaftHalfX, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 0);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.slab, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH, shaftHalfX, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 0);\n    addBox(buildingGroup, mats.slab, WORLD.SHAFT_WIDTH, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.12, 0, WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, -shaftHalfZ);\n\n    for (let f = 0; f < WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT; f += 1) {\n        const y = f * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT;\n        const floorInfo = {\n            floorNumber: f,\n            nodes: {},\n            callPanel: null,\n            shaftIndicator: null,\n            desks: [],\n            sitTargets: {}\n        };\n\n        // Intermediate floor slabs as four strips around the shaft opening.\n        if (f > 0) {\n            addBox(buildingGroup, mats.floorSlab, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH, 0.14, halfD - shaftHalfZ, 0, y - 0.07, (halfD + shaftHalfZ) / 2);\n            addBox(buildingGroup, mats.floorSlab, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH, 0.14, halfD - shaftHalfZ, 0, y - 0.07, -(halfD + shaftHalfZ) / 2);\n            addBox(buildingGroup, mats.floorSlab, halfW - shaftHalfX, 0.14, WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH, -(halfW + shaftHalfX) / 2, y - 0.07, 0);\n            addBox(buildingGroup, mats.floorSlab, halfW - shaftHalfX, 0.14, WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH, (halfW + shaftHalfX) / 2, y - 0.07, 0);\n        }\n\n        // Hallway ring around the shaft. hallS is the side in front of the doors (+Z).\n        const ring = {\n            hallS: [0, 2.6],\n            hallSE: [2.6, 2.6],\n            hallE: [2.6, 0],\n            hallNE: [2.6, -2.6],\n            hallN: [0, -2.6],\n            hallNW: [-2.6, -2.6],\n            hallW: [-2.6, 0],\n            hallSW: [-2.6, 2.6]\n        };\n        for (const name of Object.keys(ring)) addNode(floorInfo, name, ring[name][0], y, ring[name][1]);\n        const ringOrder = [\"hallS\", \"hallSE\", \"hallE\", \"hallNE\", \"hallN\", \"hallNW\", \"hallW\", \"hallSW\"];\n        for (let i = 0; i < ringOrder.length; i += 1) {\n            link(floorInfo, ringOrder[i], ringOrder[(i + 1) % ringOrder.length]);\n        }\n\n        const elevWait = addNode(floorInfo, \"elevWait\", 0, y, 2.35);\n        link(floorInfo, elevWait.name, \"hallS\");\n        floorInfo.sitTargets[\"elevWait\"] = { sit: false, facing: Math.PI };\n\n        // Call panel next to the shaft, facing +Z, plus the shaft indicator above the doors.\n        const panel = createCallPanel();\n        panel.position.set(-1.05, y + 1.25, shaftHalfZ + 0.04);\n        buildingGroup.add(panel);\n        floorInfo.callPanel = panel;\n\n        const indicator = createTextDisplay(0.9);\n        indicator.mesh.position.set(0, y + 2.6, shaftHalfZ + 0.05);\n        buildingGroup.add(indicator.mesh);\n        floorInfo.shaftIndicator = indicator;\n\n        if (f === 0) {\n            buildLobby(floorInfo, buildingGroup, mats, addNode, link, publishSeat);\n        } else {\n            buildOfficeFloor(floorInfo, buildingGroup, mats, addNode, link, publishSeat);\n        }\n\n        floors.push(floorInfo);\n    }\n\n    return {\n        buildingGroup: buildingGroup,\n        floors: floors,\n        bfsPath: bfsPath,\n        nearestNodeName: worldNearestNode\n    };\n}\n\nfunction buildOfficeFloor(floorInfo, group, mats, addNode, link, publishSeat) {\n    const y = floorInfo.floorNumber * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT;\n\n    // Interior walls: office block front partition at z = -4 with 1.2-unit doorway gaps.\n    const doorXs = [-9.5, -7.0, -3.5, 3.5];\n    let cursor = -WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH / 2;\n    for (const dx of doorXs) {\n        addBox(group, mats.innerWall, dx - 0.6 - cursor, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.12, (cursor + dx - 0.6) / 2, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, -4);\n        cursor = dx + 0.6;\n    }\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH / 2 - cursor, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.12, (cursor + WORLD.BUILDING_WIDTH / 2) / 2, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, -4);\n\n    // Office partitions running back to the rear wall.\n    for (const px of [-8.0, -5.0, -2.0, 2.0]) {\n        addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 5.0, px, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, -6.5);\n    }\n\n    // Conference room walls (front-left quadrant) with a doorway gap at z = 6.\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 3.0, -3.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 4.5);\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 3.0, -3.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 7.5);\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 8.0, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.12, -7.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 3.0);\n\n    // Lounge walls (front-right quadrant) with a doorway gap at z = 6.\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 3.0, 3.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 4.5);\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 0.12, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 3.0, 3.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 7.5);\n    addBox(group, mats.innerWall, 8.0, WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT, 0.12, 7.0, y + WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT / 2, 3.0);\n\n    // Four private offices along the back wall. Person sits facing -Z (the monitor).\n    const officeCenters = [-9.5, -6.5, -3.5, 3.5];\n    for (let i = 0; i < officeCenters.length; i += 1) {\n        const letter = String.fromCharCode(65 + i);\n        const cx = officeCenters[i];\n        const doorName = \"office\" + letter + \"_door\";\n        const deskName = \"office\" + letter + \"_desk\";\n\n        buildDesk(group, mats, cx, y, -7.2);\n        const chairFacing = Math.PI; // seat opens toward the monitor, person faces the monitor\n        buildChair(group, mats, cx, y, -6.35, chairFacing);\n\n        addNode(floorInfo, doorName, cx, y, -3.8);\n        const deskNode = addNode(floorInfo, deskName, cx, y, -6.35);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, deskName, chairFacing);\n\n        const nearestCorner = cx < -2.6 ? \"hallNW\" : (cx > 2.6 ? \"hallNE\" : \"hallN\");\n        link(floorInfo, doorName, nearestCorner);\n        link(floorInfo, doorName, deskName);\n        floorInfo.desks.push({ name: deskName, doorName: doorName, pos: deskNode.pos.clone(), facing: chairFacing });\n\n        if (i === 0) link(floorInfo, \"hallNW\", \"hallW\");\n    }\n\n    // Conference room: long table with four chairs, two per long side facing each other.\n    const confTable = [-7.0, 6.0];\n    buildTable(group, mats, confTable[0], y, confTable[1], 3.2, 1.4, 0.75);\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"conf_door\", -2.5, y, 6.0);\n    const confCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"conf_center\", -6.0, y, 6.0);\n    link(floorInfo, \"conf_door\", \"hallSW\");\n    link(floorInfo, \"conf_door\", \"conf_center\");\n\n    const confSeats = [[-8.4, 5.1], [-6.2, 5.1], [-8.4, 6.9], [-6.2, 6.9]];\n    for (let i = 0; i < confSeats.length; i += 1) {\n        const name = \"conf_seat\" + i;\n        const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(confSeats[i][0], y, confSeats[i][1]);\n        const facing = faceToward(seatPos, new THREE.Vector3(confTable[0], y, confTable[1]));\n        buildChair(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n        link(floorInfo, \"conf_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    // Lounge / break area.\n    buildTable(group, mats, 6.5, y, 6.0, 1.4, 1.4, 0.72);\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"lounge_door\", 2.5, y, 6.0);\n    const loungeCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"lounge_center\", 4.2, y, 6.0);\n    link(floorInfo, \"lounge_door\", \"hallSE\");\n    link(floorInfo, \"lounge_door\", \"lounge_center\");\n\n    const loungeSeats = [[7.2, 7.5], [4.9, 4.8], [8.6, 4.6]];\n    for (let i = 0; i < loungeSeats.length; i += 1) {\n        const name = \"lounge_spot\" + i;\n        const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(loungeSeats[i][0], y, loungeSeats[i][1]);\n        const facing = faceToward(seatPos, new THREE.Vector3(6.5, y, 6.0));\n        if (i === 0) buildCouch(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        else buildArmchair(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n        link(floorInfo, \"lounge_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    buildWaterCooler(group, mats, 10.2, y, 7.4);\n    const coolerNode = addNode(floorInfo, \"water_cooler\", 9.5, y, 6.8);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"water_cooler\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(coolerNode.pos, new THREE.Vector3(10.2, y, 7.4)) };\n    link(floorInfo, \"lounge_center\", \"water_cooler\");\n\n    // Hallway loiter spots.\n    const hallStandN = addNode(floorInfo, \"hall_stand_N\", -1.5, y, -2.6);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"hall_stand_N\"] = { sit: false, facing: 0 };\n    link(floorInfo, \"hallN\", \"hall_stand_N\");\n    const hallStandS = addNode(floorInfo, \"hall_stand_S\", 1.5, y, 2.6);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"hall_stand_S\"] = { sit: false, facing: Math.PI };\n    link(floorInfo, \"hallS\", \"hall_stand_S\");\n\n    buildPlant(group, mats, -10.4, y, 8.4);\n}\n\nfunction buildLobby(floorInfo, group, mats, addNode, link, publishSeat) {\n    const y = 0;\n\n    // Entrance chain: sidewalk -> threshold -> inside -> lobby centre -> elevator.\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"outside\", 0, y, 12);\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"front_door_threshold\", 0, y, 9.35);\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"entrance\", 0, y, 7.4);\n    const lobbyCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", 0, y, 5.8);\n    link(floorInfo, \"outside\", \"front_door_threshold\");\n    link(floorInfo, \"front_door_threshold\", \"entrance\");\n    link(floorInfo, \"entrance\", \"lobby_center\");\n    link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", \"elevWait\");\n\n    // Cafe counter on the left wall.\n    addBox(group, mats.furniture, 0.9, 1.0, 5.4, -10.6, 0.5, 5.6);\n    addBox(group, mats.counterTop, 1.0, 0.06, 5.4, -10.6, 1.02, 5.6);\n    addBox(group, mats.darkFurniture, 0.5, 0.55, 0.5, -10.6, 1.32, 4.2);   // coffee machine\n    addBox(group, new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0xc9a06a }), 0.6, 0.28, 1.2, -10.5, 1.17, 6.6); // pastry display\n\n    const cafeOrder = addNode(floorInfo, \"cafe_order\", -9.3, y, 5.6);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"cafe_order\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(cafeOrder.pos, new THREE.Vector3(-10.6, y, 5.6)) };\n\n    addNode(floorInfo, \"cafe_door\", -2.9, y, 4.2);\n    link(floorInfo, \"cafe_door\", \"hallSW\");\n    const cafeCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"cafe_center\", -5.0, y, 3.6);\n    link(floorInfo, \"cafe_door\", \"cafe_center\");\n\n    // Bistro tables with two chairs each.\n    const bistroTables = [[-7.4, 4.2], [-6.2, 6.8], [-9.0, 1.8], [-4.4, 2.4]];\n    for (let i = 0; i < bistroTables.length; i += 1) {\n        const tx = bistroTables[i][0];\n        const tz = bistroTables[i][1];\n        buildTable(group, mats, tx, y, tz, 1.1, 1.1, 0.74);\n        for (let s = 0; s < 2; s += 1) {\n            const name = \"cafe_seat\" + i + \"_\" + s;\n            const offset = s === 0 ? -0.85 : 0.85;\n            const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(tx, y, tz + offset);\n            const facing = faceToward(seatPos, new THREE.Vector3(tx, y, tz));\n            buildChair(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n            addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n            publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n            link(floorInfo, \"cafe_center\", name);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Front lounge (right side).\n    const frontTable = new THREE.Vector3(7.0, y, 6.2);\n    buildTable(group, mats, frontTable.x, y, frontTable.z, 1.4, 1.4, 0.72);\n    const frontLoungeCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"front_lounge_center\", 5.6, y, 6.2);\n    link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", \"front_lounge_center\");\n\n    const frontSeats = [[7.0, 7.8], [4.9, 5.0], [9.1, 5.0]];\n    for (let i = 0; i < frontSeats.length; i += 1) {\n        const name = \"front_lounge_seat\" + i;\n        const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(frontSeats[i][0], y, frontSeats[i][1]);\n        const facing = faceToward(seatPos, frontTable);\n        if (i === 0) buildCouch(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        else buildArmchair(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n        link(floorInfo, \"front_lounge_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    // Back lounge: two couches facing each other across a coffee table.\n    const backTable = new THREE.Vector3(5.0, y, -6.0);\n    buildTable(group, mats, backTable.x, y, backTable.z, 1.4, 1.4, 0.72);\n    const backLoungeCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"back_lounge_center\", 5.0, y, -3.6);\n    link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", \"back_lounge_center\");\n\n    const backSeats = [[5.0, -4.6], [5.0, -7.4]];\n    for (let i = 0; i < backSeats.length; i += 1) {\n        const name = i === 0 ? \"back_lounge_N\" : \"back_lounge_S\";\n        const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(backSeats[i][0], y, backSeats[i][1]);\n        const facing = faceToward(seatPos, backTable);\n        buildCouch(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n        link(floorInfo, \"back_lounge_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    // Conversation pit (back-left): round table with four armchairs.\n    const pitTable = new THREE.Vector3(-7.0, y, -6.4);\n    const roundTop = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.85, 0.85, 0.06, 18), mats.furniture);\n    roundTop.position.set(pitTable.x, 0.74, pitTable.z);\n    group.add(roundTop);\n    const pitCenter = addNode(floorInfo, \"pit_center\", -7.0, y, -3.9);\n    link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", \"pit_center\");\n\n    const pitSeats = { pit_N: [-7.0, -5.4], pit_S: [-7.0, -7.4], pit_E: [-5.6, -6.4], pit_W: [-8.4, -6.4] };\n    for (const name of Object.keys(pitSeats)) {\n        const seatPos = new THREE.Vector3(pitSeats[name][0], y, pitSeats[name][1]);\n        const facing = faceToward(seatPos, pitTable);\n        buildArmchair(group, mats, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z, facing);\n        addNode(floorInfo, name, seatPos.x, y, seatPos.z);\n        publishSeat(floorInfo, name, facing);\n        link(floorInfo, \"pit_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    // Water coolers with standing waypoints.\n    const wcFront = buildWaterCooler(group, mats, -3.6, y, 8.4);\n    const wcFrontNode = addNode(floorInfo, \"lobby_wc_front\", -2.9, y, 7.5);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"lobby_wc_front\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(wcFrontNode.pos, wcFront.position) };\n    link(floorInfo, \"entrance\", \"lobby_wc_front\");\n\n    const wcBack = buildWaterCooler(group, mats, -9.6, y, -3.4);\n    const wcBackNode = addNode(floorInfo, \"lobby_wc_back\", -8.7, y, -2.9);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"lobby_wc_back\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(wcBackNode.pos, wcBack.position) };\n    link(floorInfo, \"hallSW\", \"lobby_wc_back\");\n\n    // Reception desk tucked off to the side so it does not block entrance -> elevator.\n    addBox(group, mats.furniture, 1.6, 1.05, 0.8, -4.2, 0.525, 6.2);\n    const reception = addNode(floorInfo, \"reception\", -3.4, y, 6.2);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"reception\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(reception.pos, new THREE.Vector3(-4.2, y, 6.2)) };\n    link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", \"reception\");\n\n    // Info kiosk near the entrance.\n    addBox(group, mats.darkFurniture, 0.7, 1.2, 0.5, 3.4, 0.6, 8.2);\n    const kiosk = addNode(floorInfo, \"kiosk\", 2.6, y, 7.4);\n    floorInfo.sitTargets[\"kiosk\"] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(kiosk.pos, new THREE.Vector3(3.4, y, 8.2)) };\n    link(floorInfo, \"entrance\", \"kiosk\");\n\n    // Generic loiter waypoints so visitors spread out instead of piling up.\n    const loiter = {\n        lobby_stand_center: [1.5, 4.4],\n        lobby_stand_NE: [8.6, 7.2],\n        lobby_stand_NW: [-9.4, 7.0],\n        lobby_stand_midE: [6.4, 2.4],\n        lobby_stand_midW: [-6.4, 2.4],\n        lobby_stand_entry: [1.8, 6.4]\n    };\n    for (const name of Object.keys(loiter)) {\n        const node = addNode(floorInfo, name, loiter[name][0], y, loiter[name][1]);\n        floorInfo.sitTargets[name] = { sit: false, facing: faceToward(node.pos, new THREE.Vector3(0, y, 2.4)) };\n        link(floorInfo, \"lobby_center\", name);\n    }\n\n    // Potted plants by the entrance (kept clear of the 3-unit doorway).\n    buildPlant(group, mats, -2.6, y, 8.4);\n    buildPlant(group, mats, 2.6, y, 8.4);\n\n    floorInfo.entranceSpot = \"front_door_threshold\";\n    floorInfo.cafeSpots = Object.keys(floorInfo.nodes).filter((n) => n.indexOf(\"cafe_seat\") === 0);\n    floorInfo.frontLoungeSpots = Object.keys(floorInfo.sitTargets).filter((n) => n.indexOf(\"front_lounge_seat\") === 0);\n    floorInfo.backLoungeSpots = [\"back_lounge_N\", \"back_lounge_S\"];\n    floorInfo.pitSpots = [\"pit_N\", \"pit_S\", \"pit_E\", \"pit_W\"];\n    floorInfo.loiterSpots = Object.keys(loiter);\n    floorInfo.standingSpots = [\"cafe_order\", \"reception\", \"kiosk\", \"lobby_wc_front\", \"lobby_wc_back\"];\n}\n\nwindow.WORLD = WORLD;\nwindow.bfsPath = bfsPath;\nwindow.createWorld = createWorld;\nwindow.worldNearestNode = worldNearestNode;\n","path":"C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/world.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"lmstudio","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-gsq-rco","usage":{"input":62311,"output":15547,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5054,"totalTokens":77858,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791659250707,"responseId":"chatcmpl-s6zo4n9yigf4tee6ya2u27","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":3205302,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"QVbHs6bzzNM5hVuUsVA5j5VbAkKnh4JL","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/world.js"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1791662456016},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: `buildLobby` is called before its declaration in createWorld — function declarations are hoisted ✓.\n\nAlso `floorInfo.sitTargets[name] = {sit:false, facing}` for standing waypoints ✓.\n\nWait, in buildOfficeFloor I wrote `if (i === 0) link(floorInfo, \"hallNW\", \"hallW\");` inside loop — redundant but harmless.\n\nNow elevator.js.\n\nCar geometry: group at (0, pos*floorHeight, 0). Frame yellow semi-transparent opacity .5; back wall opaque yellow. Doors on +Z face each half width (car width = SHAFT_WIDTH=3 → halves 1.5). Door panels height 2.2, thickness 0.06, more opaque (0.7).\n\nClosed: left door center x=-0.75, right +0.75 at z = shaftHalfZ? The car occupies the shaft; doors on +Z face at z=1.47 (just inside shaft boundary). Let's set car interior from -1.4..1.4 in x and z with walls thickness 0.08. Door plane at z = 1.45.\n\nOpen: each slides outward by (carWidth/2 - gap) ≈ 1.4 → left door center at -1.4? That would put the panel beyond the side wall. Real sliding doors slide into pockets; visually, offset to x = ±(0.75 + 1.3) hmm. Let's define openOffset = carWidth/2 - 0.15 = 1.35 → left door center at -0.75 - ... Actually spec: \"Open: each half slides outward by ~(car width / 2 - small gap)\" i.e., displacement ≈ 1.4. So left door center = -0.75 - 1.4 = -2.15 which is outside the car (pocket). Hmm, that would look odd but it's what spec says; typical visual: doors slide to sides overlapping the frame. I'll use displacement = carWidth/2 - 0.15 = 1.35 → left at -2.1, right +2.1 — beyond shaft walls (which are at x=±1.5). Doors would poke through side walls visually. Better: displacement such that doors stack just inside the side walls: max center = ±(1.5-0.75)=±0.75... no, door half-width 0.75 so center can be at most ±(1.5-0.75) = 0.75 → fully open means doors flush against side walls with centers at ±0.75 — that's exactly the closed position meeting at x=0? No: closed, left door spans -1.5..0 (center -0.75). Open, it must slide to cover... there's no room; a real car has pockets in the wall. So visually, doors sliding \"outward\" beyond the shaft is normal because they'd be hidden in the wall pockets. I'll allow displacement up to 1.2 so doors extend slightly past the shaft sides — acceptable since walls are transparent and doors draw after building (renderOrder 1).\n\nLet me use openOffset = carWidth/2 - 0.15 = 1.35, i.e., door centers at ±(0.75+1.35)=±2.1? Hmm that's a lot. Let me instead define: closed center ±0.75; open center ±(carWidth/2 + 0.4)?? I'll just use displacement = carWidth/2 - 0.15 = 1.35 as spec says, giving open centers at ±2.1. Since the shaft is a hole and doors are transparent-ish, it reads as doors retracted into pockets. Fine — but they'd overlap the shaft side walls (transparent) → visually acceptable.\n\nHmm, maybe better: displacement = carWidth/2 - 0.35 = 1.15 → open centers ±1.9. I'll go with spec formula ~1.35. Actually let me reduce to keep it tidy: use `openOffset = carWidth / 2 - 0.2` and place door panels at z=1.45; open center = ±(carWidth/4 + openOffset) = ±(0.75+1.3)=±1.55. Hmm that means doors just barely past the wall line. Whatever, I'll use displacement 1.2 → centers ±1.95.\n\nLet me define: closedCenter = ±carHalfWidth/2 = ±0.75; openCenter = ±(carHalfWidth + carHalfWidth - 0.3)?? Let's simply compute doorOpenFraction f: center = ±(0.75 + f * (1.4)). Where 1.4 ≈ car width/2 - small gap ✓ matches spec. Good, so max center ±2.15.\n\nDestination panel on back-right wall with one glowing cylinder button per floor; store refs. Buttons light when pressed (destinations has floor).\n\nIn-car indicator plane 0.6x0.6 above doors inside, facing -Z (visible to passengers) → position z = -1.4? The doors are at +Z face; \"mounted above the doors from the INSIDE of the car, so riders can see the current floor\" → place at z=1.35 (just inside door plane), y=2.6, rotated to face -Z (rotation.y = π).\n\nCar group children renderOrder 1.\n\nAdapter class Elevator:\n- constructor(scene, world): store world; logic = new ElevatorLogic({floorCount: WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT, maxCapacity:4, floorHeight:WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT}); build geometry.\n- methods delegate to logic; also mirror properties via getters? Spec says \"Mirror/read through logic state such as state, direction...\" — I'll expose accessor methods and also copy fields after tick (e.g., `this.state = logic.state` each tick) so HUD can read elevator.state ✓. Simplest: assign mirrored fields in tick.\n\nAlso need `spotToWorld(spot)` → Vector3 world position; `doorThresholdWorld(agentFloor, spotX)`.\n\nCall panel lamps update: for each floor's callPanel: setUp(upCalls.has(f)), setDown(downCalls.has(f)), setIndicator(text). Shaft indicator shows car's current floor & direction e.g. \"3^\". Use logic.displayText().\n\nAlso in-car indicator text.\n\nLet me write elevator.js.\n\nCareful with duplicate top-level names across files: `Elevator` class ✓ unique; helper functions inside methods only, or unique names like `buildCarGeometry`. Avoid re-declaring `WORLD` (it's a const in world.js — referencing it in elevator.js is fine as ref resolves via projectGlobals ✓).\n\nAlso careful: static checker flags duplicate top-level let/const/class across classic scripts. In elevator.js I must not declare `const STATES` if world.js has none... person.js declares consts PERSON_*, world.js declares WORLD, SEAT_DROP. elevator_logic.js has no root-level const (all inside IIFE) ✓. So in elevator.js avoid names: WORLD, SEAT_DROP, PERSON_*, and sim.js must avoid all of those too.\n\nLet me write elevator.js now.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now the visual elevator adapter.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"E9pdFALjCr04SNR2d0G9vT23phvHdsT1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// elevator.js - Three.js car + doors + indicators, as an adapter around ElevatorLogic.\n// All scheduling/state decisions live in ElevatorLogic; this file only renders them.\n\nconst CAR_WIDTH = WORLD.SHAFT_WIDTH;\nconst CAR_DEPTH = WORLD.SHAFT_DEPTH;\nconst CAR_HEIGHT = 2.4;\nconst DOOR_HALF_W = CAR_WIDTH / 2;\nconst DOOR_HEIGHT = 2.15;\nconst DOOR_SLIDE_MAX = CAR_WIDTH / 2 - 0.15;\n\nfunction elevatorMaterials() {\n    return {\n        frame: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0xf4c531, opacity: 0.5, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        door: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({\n            color: 0xe8b92f, opacity: 0.7, transparent: true, depthWrite: false, side: THREE.DoubleSide\n        }),\n        solidBack: new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({ color: 0xd9a520, side: THREE.DoubleSide })\n    };\n}\n\nclass Elevator {\n    constructor(scene, world) {\n        this.world = world;\n        this.logic = new ElevatorLogic({\n            floorCount: WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT,\n            maxCapacity: 4,\n            floorHeight: WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT\n        });\n\n        const mats = elevatorMaterials();\n        this.mats = mats;\n\n        this.carGroup = new THREE.Group();\n        scene.add(this.carGroup);\n\n        function addCarPart(mesh) {\n            mesh.renderOrder = 1;\n            return mesh;\n        }\n\n        // Car floor and ceiling\n        const carFloor = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(CAR_WIDTH, 0.08, CAR_DEPTH), mats.frame));\n        carFloor.position.y = -0.04;\n        this.carGroup.add(carFloor);\n\n        const carCeiling = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(CAR_WIDTH, 0.08, CAR_DEPTH), mats.frame));\n        carCeiling.position.y = CAR_HEIGHT;\n        this.carGroup.add(carCeiling);\n\n        // Side walls + solid back wall\n        for (const side of [-1, 1]) {\n            const wall = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.06, CAR_HEIGHT, CAR_DEPTH), mats.frame));\n            wall.position.set(side * (CAR_WIDTH / 2 - 0.03), CAR_HEIGHT / 2, 0);\n            this.carGroup.add(wall);\n        }\n\n        const backWall = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(CAR_WIDTH, CAR_HEIGHT, 0.06), mats.solidBack));\n        backWall.position.set(0, CAR_HEIGHT / 2, -(CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.03));\n        this.carGroup.add(backWall);\n\n        // Two sliding doors on the +Z face\n        this.leftDoor = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(DOOR_HALF_W, DOOR_HEIGHT, 0.06), mats.door));\n        this.rightDoor = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(DOOR_HALF_W, DOOR_HEIGHT, 0.06), mats.door));\n        this.leftDoor.position.set(-DOOR_HALF_W / 2, DOOR_HEIGHT / 2, CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.03);\n        this.rightDoor.position.set(DOOR_HALF_W / 2, DOOR_HEIGHT / 2, CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.03);\n        this.carGroup.add(this.leftDoor);\n        this.carGroup.add(this.rightDoor);\n\n        // Destination panel on the back-right wall with one glowing button per floor\n        this.buttonPanel = new THREE.Group();\n        const panelPlate = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.7, 1.5, 0.04), mats.solidBack));\n        panelPlate.position.set(0, 0, 0);\n        this.buttonPanel.add(panelPlate);\n\n        this.buttons = [];\n        const buttonOnMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xffd23f });\n        const buttonOffMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x5a4a17 });\n        for (let f = 0; f < WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT; f += 1) {\n            const button = addCarPart(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.06, 0.06, 0.03, 12), buttonOffMat));\n            button.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\n            button.position.set(-0.18 + (f % 3) * 0.18, 0.45 - Math.floor(f / 3) * 0.35, 0.03);\n            this.buttonPanel.add(button);\n            this.buttons.push({ mesh: button, floor: f, onMat: buttonOnMat, offMat: buttonOffMat });\n        }\n\n        this.buttonPanel.position.set(1.0, 1.4, -(CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.06));\n        this.buttonPanel.rotation.y = Math.PI;\n        this.carGroup.add(this.buttonPanel);\n\n        // In-car floor indicator above the doors, facing back at the passengers\n        this.inCarDisplay = createTextDisplay(0.6);\n        this.inCarDisplay.mesh.position.set(0, CAR_HEIGHT - 0.35, CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.08);\n        this.inCarDisplay.mesh.rotation.y = Math.PI;\n        this.inCarDisplay.mesh.renderOrder = 1;\n        this.carGroup.add(this.inCarDisplay.mesh);\n\n        // Mirror logic state for the HUD\n        this.state = this.logic.state;\n        this.direction = this.logic.direction;\n        this.currentFloor = this.logic.currentFloor;\n        this.targetFloor = this.logic.targetFloor;\n    }\n\n    callUp(floor) { this.logic.callUp(floor); }\n    callDown(floor) { this.logic.callDown(floor); }\n    pressDestination(floor) { this.logic.pressDestination(floor); }\n    isAcceptingAt(floor, direction) { return this.logic.isAcceptingAt(floor, direction); }\n    currentCapacityFree() { return this.logic.currentCapacityFree(); }\n    reserveBoardingSpot(person) { return this.logic.reserveBoardingSpot(person); }\n    completeBoard(person) { return this.logic.completeBoard(person); }\n    registerDisembark(person) { return this.logic.registerDisembark(person); }\n    completeDisembark(person) { return this.logic.completeDisembark(person); }\n    tick(dt) {\n        this.logic.tick(dt);\n        this.updateVisuals();\n    }\n    reset() {\n        this.logic.reset();\n        this.updateVisuals();\n    }\n\n    // Logical interior spot -> world position (car-local spots are converted here).\n    spotToWorld(spot) {\n        return new THREE.Vector3(spot.x, this.carGroup.position.y + spot.y, spot.z);\n    }\n\n    doorThresholdWorld(floor, x) {\n        const baseY = floor * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT;\n        return new THREE.Vector3(x, baseY, CAR_DEPTH / 2 - 0.15);\n    }\n\n    updateVisuals() {\n        this.carGroup.position.y = this.logic.carPos * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT;\n\n        const openFraction = this.logic.doorOpenFraction();\n        const slide = DOOR_SLIDE_MAX * openFraction;\n        this.leftDoor.position.x = -DOOR_HALF_W / 2 - slide;\n        this.rightDoor.position.x = DOOR_HALF_W / 2 + slide;\n\n        const text = this.logic.displayText();\n\n        for (let f = 0; f < WORLD.FLOOR_COUNT; f += 1) {\n            const floorInfo = this.world.floors[f];\n            if (!floorInfo || !floorInfo.callPanel) continue;\n            const upOn = this.logic.upCalls.has(f);\n            const downOn = this.logic.downCalls.has(f);\n            const panel = floorInfo.callPanel;\n            if (panel.userData.upOn !== upOn) {\n                panel.userData.setUp(upOn);\n                panel.userData.upOn = upOn;\n            }\n            if (panel.userData.downOn !== downOn) {\n                panel.userData.setDown(downOn);\n                panel.userData.downOn = downOn;\n            }\n            panel.userData.setIndicator(text);\n            floorInfo.shaftIndicator.setIndicator(text);\n        }\n\n        for (const button of this.buttons) {\n            const on = this.logic.destinations.has(button.floor);\n            button.mesh.material = on ? button.onMat : button.offMat;\n        }\n\n        this.inCarDisplay.setIndicator(text);\n\n        // Mirrored state for the HUD\n        this.state = this.logic.state;\n        this.direction = this.logic.direction;\n        this.currentFloor = Math.round(this.logic.carPos);\n        this.targetFloor = this.logic.targetFloor;\n    }\n}\n\nwindow.Elevator = Elevator;\n","path":"C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/elevator.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"lmstudio","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-gsq-rco","usage":{"input":77911,"output":3702,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1590,"totalTokens":81613,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791662456019,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0r4103c4r84aqmqoos3ioh","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":853084,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"E9pdFALjCr04SNR2d0G9vT23phvHdsT1","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to C:/Users/Jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco_office_prompt_v3/elevator.js"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":1,"timestamp":1791663309107},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: `createTextDisplay` is defined in world.js as a function declaration → global ✓ resolves via projectGlobals.\n\nNow sim.js — the big one. Let me write it carefully.\n\nKey components:\n1. Globals: scene, camera, renderer, controls, world, elevator, clock, agents, seatReservations, targetOccupancy, hud refs, sun/ambient/hemi light refs.\n2. Clock object with tick(realDt), format(), getDelta().\n3. Lighting keyframes + applyLighting(simHour).\n4. Agent creation & schedules.\n5. Plan compilers.\n6. Action dispatch (startAction / processAction).\n7. Collision resolver.\n8. topUpVisitors, applyOccupancy.\n9. HUD build/update.\n10. Render loop + startup call.\n\nLet me define constants: WALK_SPEED = 1.3; NAMES list.\n\nAgent structure:\n```js\nfunction makeAgent(id, role) {\n  return {\n    id, name, role, group:null, inScene:false,\n    homeFloor, deskId, deskWpName, deskDoorWpName,\n    floor:0, state:'AWAY', plan:[], actionIndex:0, currentAction:null,\n    hasLunched:false, arrivalTime, lunchTime, lunchDuration, departureTime, plannedMeetingTimes:[],\n    path:[], pathIndex:0, seatKey:null, walkPhase...\n  };\n}\n```\n\nActions: {type, floor, wpName, dir, toFloor, minutes}.\n\nstartAction(agent, action): switch on type; for WAIT_SIM resolve untilMin.\n\nprocessAction(agent, motionDt) returns true when complete.\n\nDispatch loop in updateAgent: up to 16 iterations:\n```js\nfor (let guard = 0; guard < 16; guard++) {\n   if (!agent.currentAction) { advancePlan(agent); if (!agent.currentAction) break; }\n   if (processAction(agent, motionDt)) { agent.currentAction = null; ... } else break;\n}\n```\nWhere advancePlan takes next action from plan and calls startAction.\n\nCareful: processAction for WALK_TO_WP does actual movement work; if it returns false we break out of the loop ✓ (movement done once per frame).\n\nLet me write helper functions:\n\n- `floorBaseY(floor)` = floor * WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT.\n- `agentWorldPos(agent)`.\n\nWALK_TO_WP handling:\n```js\nfunction startWalkAction(agent, action) {\n  const nodes = world.floors[action.floor].nodes;\n  const startName = world.nearestNodeName(nodes, agent.group.position);\n  if (!startName) return false;\n  agent.path = bfsPath(nodes, startName, action.wpName);\n  agent.pathIndex = 0;\n  agent.walkFloor = action.floor;\n}\n```\nHmm: nearest node may be far from the agent (e.g., sitting at a chair node ✓ that's a node). Good.\n\nprocessWalk(agent, motionDt):\n```js\nif (!agent.path.length) return true;\nconst target = agent.path[agent.pathIndex];\n// move in XZ toward target\nconst dx = target.x - pos.x, dz = target.z - pos.z;\nconst dist = Math.hypot(dx,dz);\nif (dist < 0.25) { agent.pathIndex++; if (index >= len) return true; continue-ish }\nelse move: pos.x += dx/dist * speed*motionDt etc.\n```\nStall detection with _prevWp and _stallT as spec.\n\nSet userData.isWalking = true, isSitting=false during walk; ensure group y = floorBaseY (unless sitting? walking means standing) ✓ set y = baseY when starting walk.\n\nFacing: rotation.y = atan2(dx,dz) toward movement direction ✓.\n\nCollision exemption for entrance chain: \"During WALK_TO_WP for the entrance chain, exempt agents from crowd collision against other agents until they clear the threshold into the lobby.\" Implement flag `agent.exemptCollision` set true when action is WALK_TO_WP with wpName in {outside, front_door_threshold, entrance} (or while agent is outside/threshold), cleared once at lobby_center/entrance reached. Simpler: in applyCollisions skip agents whose currentAction.type === 'WALK_TO_WP' && entranceChain includes wpName... but \"until they clear the threshold into the lobby\" — so exempt if action.wpName is one of outside/front_door_threshold/entrance, or agent.position.z > 9 (outside). I'll implement helper `isEntranceChain(agent)`.\n\nAlso stall recovery for entrance chain: \"If an arriving or leaving agent makes <0.005/frame of progress near front_door_threshold for >1.5 motion-seconds, advance it to the next entrance waypoint.\" Implement in walk processing: if stalled and near threshold → skip to next waypoint (already generic stall skip advances path index) ✓ plus special-case: if agent is outside and target is threshold, allow teleport-ish skip. The generic stall handling covers it.\n\nENTER_ELEVATOR phases as described. Need `agent.spot` from reserve; store spotIndex for later.\n\nPRESS_FLOOR: pressDestination + complete immediately.\n\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: until elevator.logic.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===floor. Note while in car, agent stays at its spot (no movement). Should also handle if the car is at floor already.\n\nEXIT_ELEVATOR: start → registerDisembark; phase 'walkDoor': move within car-local space toward door threshold local (spot.x, 0, CAR_DEPTH/2 - 0.15); when reached, reparent to scene preserving world pos; then walk along path from elevWait node... Actually spec: \"walk to elevWait on the target floor; completeDisembark\". So after reparenting, set agent.path = [nodes['elevWait'].pos] and walk there; upon arrival → completeDisembark → done.\n\nImplementation detail: processExitElevator each frame moves agent in car-local coords toward door; then reparent; then continue walking in world space to elevWait. I'll implement as phases with a small state machine on the action object.\n\nSIT: snap to sit target position (with jitter for standing waypoints), apply facing, isSitting=true, y = baseY - SEAT_DROP ✓ (SEAT_DROP const from world.js — global ✓).\n\nSTAND: clear sitting; restore y.\n\nRELEASE_SEAT: delete seat key.\n\nENTER_STATE(state): set state.\n\nWAIT_SIM(minutes): untilMin resolved at startAction.\n\nEXIT_BUILDING: remove group from parent, inScene=false, state GONE, release seat.\n\nMARK_LUNCHED.\n\nPICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY: chooseNextActivity(agent) → sets plan; the action itself completes immediately. Note: chooseNextActivity returns a plan; we set agent.plan = plan; agent.actionIndex=0; then dispatch loop continues to next action ✓.\n\nCareful: PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY processed inside processAction; must not mutate while iterating incorrectly — I'll handle in processAction by setting agent.plan and index, returning true.\n\nNow chooseNextActivity per spec order with weights.\n\nPlan compilers as described. Let me write them.\n\nHelper `planTravelToFloorAndWp(agent, floor, wpName)`: if agent.floor !== floor → elevator actions (call direction based on relative floor; from current position walk to elevWait first). Note when already inside car? Not applicable at plan compile time.\n\nLet's define action constructors:\n```js\nfunction actWalk(floor, wpName) { return { type:'WALK_TO_WP', floor, wpName }; }\nfunction actWaitPanel(floor, dir, toFloor) {...}\nfunction actEnter(toFloor) {...}\nfunction actPress(floor) {...}\nfunction actWaitFor(floor) {...}\nfunction actExit(toFloor) {...}\nfunction actSit(floor, wpName) {...}\nfunction actStand() {...}\nfunction actReleaseSeat(key) {...}\nfunction actWaitSim(minutes) {...}\nfunction actEnterState(state) {...}\n```\n\nPlan compilers:\n\nplanArriveToDesk(agent):\n```\n[actWalk(0,'front_door_threshold'), actWalk(0,'entrance'), actWalk(0,'lobby_center'),\n actWaitPanel(0, 1, homeFloor), actEnter(homeFloor), actPress(homeFloor), actWaitFor(homeFloor), actExit(homeFloor),\n actWalk(homeFloor, deskDoorWpName), actWalk(homeFloor, deskWpName), actSit(0? homeFloor, deskWpName), ENTER_STATE('AT_DESK'), WAIT_SIM(work 20-60), PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY]\n```\nReserve seat for desk at compile time (seat key `floor:wp`).\n\nplanGoToLunch(agent): from desk: STAND, release own desk seat? The worker's desk reservation should be held while away? If released, a visitor could take... visitors don't go to office desks. Keep it simple: keep the desk reservation during lunch and re-sit at desk after; but spec says release via RELEASE_SEAT after post-meeting STAND for meeting seats. For desks I'll reserve permanently (own desk) — no conflict since only the owner uses it. Actually planGoToLunch starts with STAND then walk to office door → elevator down → lobby bistro chair (reserve a cafe seat at compile time; if none free, fall back to loiter). Then sit & eat lunchDuration → MARK_LUNCHED → elevator back up → desk → SIT(desk) → ENTER_STATE('AT_DESK') → WAIT_SIM(15-40) → PICK_NEXT.\n\nplanVisitLounge(agent): STAND, walk to lounge on same floor (or lobby if floor 0), sit 5-12 min, then return to desk.\n\nplanAttendMeeting(agent): pick meeting floor (65% home floor else random 1..5); reserve a conf seat; if all four taken → fall back to lounge plan. Walk/travel there, sit in conf seat 22-45 min, STAND, RELEASE_SEAT, return to own desk & sit.\n\nplanVisitCoworker(agent): pick random agent currently AT_DESK (role WORKER, not self); walk/ride to stand by their office door for 6-18 min; return to own desk.\n\nplanLeaveBuilding(agent): STAND + release seat; travel to lobby; walk lobby_center → entrance → front_door_threshold → outside → EXIT_BUILDING.\n\nplanVisitorVisit(agent): weighted die; then exit chain.\n\nNow, the elevator ride in plans: for a visitor going up to an office-floor lounge: WAIT_AT_PANEL(0,+1,f), ENTER_ELEVATOR(f), PRESS_FLOOR(f), WAIT_FOR_FLOOR(f), EXIT_ELEVATOR(f), walk to lounge seat, sit, then return: STAND, walk to elevWait on floor f, WAIT_AT_PANEL(f,-1,0), ENTER_ELEVATOR(0), PRESS_FLOOR(0), WAIT_FOR_FLOOR(0), EXIT_ELEVATOR(0)...\n\nNote: when riding down from an office floor, the agent must be at elevWait and press DOWN. The plan compiler should include WALK_TO_WP(floor,'elevWait') before WAIT_AT_PANEL ✓.\n\nImportant subtlety: WAIT_AT_PANEL requires `isAcceptingAt` — which requires DOOR_OPEN at that floor with matching direction (or no stops ahead). If the car arrives at floor f going up and there's a passenger wanting to get out, our agent waiting outside won't board until... fine.\n\nAnother subtlety: an agent inside the car must have its destination registered via PRESS_FLOOR; but if the agent boards and the elevator has already picked a target (e.g., it was heading elsewhere), the destination is added and will be served in that direction ✓.\n\nEdge case: agent boards at floor 0 going up, presses floor 3. Car's direction +1 → serves 3 ✓.\n\nNow, when an agent is inside the car and its WAIT_FOR_FLOOR completes (doors open), then EXIT_ELEVATOR registers disembark immediately (dispatch loop ensures same frame) ✓.\n\nAnother important detail: `isAcceptingAt` for a rider waiting at panel — after doors open at floor 0 with direction +1... but initially direction is 0 until the car moves. In our logic, when idle and call at current floor → arriveAt(0) sets state DOOR_OPENING; serveCurrentFloor clears calls; direction remains 0 → isAcceptingAt(floor, dir): `direction === 0 || this.direction === 0 || direction === this.direction` → true ✓ (car direction 0 accepts anyone). Good.\n\nBut careful: WAIT_AT_PANEL completes only when accepting AND capacity free. Then ENTER_ELEVATOR reserve phase requires isAcceptingAt again — but by then the doors may have closed and the car left; we re-press call each frame in reserve phase ✓, and if not accepting, wait (the agent stands at panel). Hmm, but the action's walk-to-door phase would be stuck. Let me handle: in ENTER_ELEVATOR reserve phase, if not accepting → keep pressing and stand still (or walk back to elevWait node). Fine.\n\nPotential deadlock: pendingBoarders non-empty holds doors open until MAX; if an agent reserved a spot but then its action gets replaced... we should ensure completeBoard happens. Stall recovery teleports to threshold forcing completion ✓.\n\nNow, the collision resolver must skip agents in car and ENTER_ELEVATOR agents ✓ and sitting agents ✓.\n\nRender loop:\n```js\nfunction animate() {\n  requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n  const realDt = Math.min(0.05, clock.getDelta());\n  clock.tick(realDt);\n  applyLighting(clock.simHour());\n  const motionDt = realDt * clock.timeScale;\n  elevator.tick(motionDt);\n  for (const agent of agents) updateAgent(agent, motionDt);\n  topUpVisitors();\n  applyCollisions();\n  for (const agent of agents) if (agent.inScene) animatePersonWalking(agent.group, motionDt);\n  controls.update();\n  renderer.render(scene, camera);\n  updateHUD();\n}\n```\n\nClock.getDelta uses performance.now().\n\nDay wrap: in clock.tick, if simMinute >= 1440 → newDay(): reset agents (fresh schedules), clear elevator sets & reset(), honor targetOccupancy.\n\nLet me write `newDay()`:\n- for each agent: if id < targetOccupancy → re-roll schedule, state = 'AWAY' (or DISABLED if beyond), remove from scene; else state='DISABLED'.\n- clear seatReservations.\n- elevator.reset().\n\nAlso agents currently in scene get removed at day wrap ✓.\n\nHUD: build DOM panel with time display, speed slider (log stops), occupancy slider, breakdown div. Update every frame but throttle text updates.\n\nLet me now write sim.js fully. I'll be careful about variable naming collisions with world.js/person.js globals: WORLD, SEAT_DROP, PERSON_*, bfsPath, createWorld, worldNearestNode, createPerson, animatePersonWalking, Elevator, ElevatorLogic, plus elevator.js consts CAR_WIDTH etc. So in sim.js avoid those names.\n\nNames I'll use in sim.js: MAX_WORKERS, MAX_VISITORS, MAX_OCCUPANCY, DEFAULT_OCCUPANCY, WALK_SPEED, MEETING_PROB, NAMES, scene, camera, renderer, controls, world, elevator, clock, agents, seatReservations, targetOccupancy, hudRefs, sunLight, ambientLight, hemiLight, DAY_KEYS.\n\nCareful: `world` vs `WORLD` — static checker treats them as distinct identifiers; `world` declared in sim.js ✓ no duplicate.\n\nLet me write it. I'll aim for ~600 lines.\n\nDetails on processAction implementation:\n\n```js\nfunction startAction(agent, action) {\n    agent.currentAction = action;\n    switch (action.type) {\n        case 'WALK_TO_WP': beginWalk(agent, action); break;\n        case 'WAIT_SIM': action.untilMin = clock.simMinute + action.minutes; break;\n        case 'ENTER_ELEVATOR': action.phase = 'reserve'; break;\n        case 'EXIT_ELEVATOR': action.phase = 'walkDoor'; elevator.registerDisembark(agent); break;\n        ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nprocessAction returns true when the action is complete.\n\nLet me write each:\n\nWALK_TO_WP:\n```js\nfunction processWalk(agent, motionDt) {\n    const path = agent.path;\n    if (!path || path.length === 0) return true;\n    if (agent.pathIndex >= path.length) return true;\n    const target = path[agent.pathIndex];\n    const pos = agent.group.position;\n    // If parented to car, shouldn't happen.\n    const dx = target.x - pos.x, dz = target.z - pos.z;\n    const dist = Math.sqrt(dx*dx+dz*dz);\n    if (dist < 0.28) {\n        agent.pathIndex += 1;\n        if (agent.pathIndex >= path.length) return true;\n        return false;   // continue next segment next iteration\n    }\n    const step = WALK_SPEED * motionDt;\n    pos.x += (dx/dist)*step; pos.z += (dz/dist)*step;\n    agent.group.rotation.y = Math.atan2(dx, dz);\n    agent.group.userData.isWalking = true;\n    stall tracking...\n    return false;\n}\n```\nStall: compare progress with `_prevWp` distance travelled per frame: track `agent._lastDist` and `agent._stallT`. If dist (remaining) decreased by < 0.005 for >1.2 motion-seconds → skip waypoint.\n\nImplement:\n```js\nif (agent._prevRemaining !== undefined && dist < agent._prevRemaining - 0.005 ... )\n```\nSimpler per spec: track progress = previous remaining distance; if (prevRemaining - dist) < 0.005 → stallT += motionDt else stallT=0; if stallT > 1.2 → advance pathIndex, reset stallT.\n\nCareful: when the agent is pushed by collisions, dist may increase — that's fine, resets stall.\n\nAlso y position during walk: set pos.y = baseY (for scene-parented agents). For car-local walking inside ENTER_ELEVATOR we handle separately.\n\nNow `beginWalk` requires agent in scene. If agent group parent isn't scene (in car), shouldn't happen.\n\nSIT handling with seat jitter for standing waypoints:\n```js\nfunction processSit(agent, action) {\n    const floorInfo = world.floors[action.floor];\n    const target = floorInfo.sitTargets[action.wpName] || {sit:false, facing:0};\n    const node = floorInfo.nodes[action.wpName];\n    if (!node) return true;\n    let x = node.pos.x, z = node.pos.z;\n    if (!target.sit) {  // standing waypoint: jitter ring so two visitors don't snap to identical coords\n        const angle = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;\n        const radius = 0.35 + Math.random() * 0.4;\n        x += Math.cos(angle)*radius; z += Math.sin(angle)*radius;\n    }\n    agent.group.position.set(x, action.floor*WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT - (target.sit ? SEAT_DROP : 0), z);\n    agent.group.rotation.y = target.facing;\n    if (target.sit) { agent.group.userData.isSitting = true; agent.group.userData.isWalking=false; }\n    else agent.group.userData.isSitting = false;\n    return true;\n}\n```\nHmm for standing waypoints, y should be baseY ✓.\n\nWait: SIT at a standing waypoint means \"stand there\" — the spec says SIT with standing waypoint jitters position. So handle both in one action ✓ (isSitting only when target.sit).\n\nSTAND: isSitting=false; restore y = parent===elevator.carGroup ? 0 : baseY.\n\nNow, agents sitting at a chair keep their group position; collisions skip them ✓ but walkers may push through them — acceptable.\n\nENTER_ELEVATOR processing:\n```js\nfunction processEnterElevator(agent, action) {\n    if (action.phase === 'reserve') {\n        pressHallCall(agent.floor, agent.dir);   // re-press in case cleared\n        if (!elevator.isAcceptingAt(agent.floor, agent.dir)) return false;\n        const spot = elevator.reserveBoardingSpot(agent);\n        if (!spot) return false;\n        action.spotIndex = spot.index;\n        action.phase = 'walkDoor';\n        return false;\n    }\n    if (action.phase === 'walkDoor') {\n        // walk in world space toward the door threshold at x = spotWorld.x\n        const spotWorld = elevator.spotToWorld(action.spotIndex? ...);\n```\nCareful: `spotToWorld(spot)` expects spot object; I'll store `action.spot = spot` (plain object) ✓.\n\nwalkDoor phase: target world point = (spotWorld.x, baseY, CAR_DEPTH/2 - 0.1). Move toward it; when close to the door plane (z >= CAR_DEPTH/2 - 0.35) → reparent to car and set local position at spot coords... Actually should walk into the car: target is inside threshold; once agent's z passes the door line, reparent.\n\nThen phase 'walkSpot': move in car-local space toward spot (x,z); when close → completeBoard → return true.\n\nStall recovery in walkDoor: track _prevWalk/_stallT; after 1.5 motion-seconds of no progress → teleport to threshold and force-complete the phase ✓.\n\nAlso must ensure agent stands (isSitting false) while boarding ✓.\n\nFacing inside car: turn to face doors (rotation.y = 0) upon completion ✓.\n\nNow, `agent.dir` for ENTER_ELEVATOR — plan compiler sets it; but spec says preserve toFloor and don't infer destination from direction. I'll store action.dir from the plan compile (the direction of travel) ✓.\n\nPRESS_FLOOR: elevator.pressDestination(action.floor); return true.\n\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: if state DOOR_OPEN && currentFloor === floor → complete. Note: use elevator.currentFloor mirrored = Math.round(carPos) ✓.\n\nEXIT_ELEVATOR phases as described.\n\nNow, the \"seatReservations\" key format `\"floor:wpName\"`.\n\nreserveSeat(floor, wpName): key; if exists return false; add and store agent.seatKey.\n\nRelease in RELEASE_SEAT action, end-of-day override, day-wrap.\n\nEnd-of-day override: in updateAgent daily schedule processing: \"replan to planLeaveBuilding if past departure and not already heading home\". Implement: if simMinute >= departureTime && state !== 'LEAVING' && currentAction type not part of leaving → replace plan with planLeaveBuilding(agent) (which includes STAND + RELEASE_SEAT).\n\nNow spawn logic for AWAY agents: when clock.simMinute >= arrivalTime and within business hours (say 7..21), spawn: add group to scene at outside node with jitter, state = 'AWAY'→ then set plan. For visitors, topUpVisitors re-arms them.\n\nLet me define `spawnAgent(agent)`:\n```js\nif (!agent.group) agent.group = createPerson();  // build full pool at startup: create groups for all agents at startup (spec says always build the full pool at startup). So create group for each agent at startup but only add to scene when present.\n```\n\"Always build the full pool at startup so roles + desk assignments stay stable; the slider moves agents between AWAY (normal lifecycle) and a parked DISABLED state (invisible, never spawns...)\". So create person meshes for all 100 at startup ✓ (100 groups is fine).\n\nSpawn: add group to scene, position at outside node with jitter ±1.1 x, ±0.75 z; set plan = role WORKER ? planArriveToDesk : planVisitorVisit; state 'ARRIVING'.\n\nFor workers: they arrive once per day (state AWAY until arrivalTime). For visitors: recycled by topUpVisitors.\n\ncountPresent(): agents whose state is present in building (not AWAY/GONE/DISABLED).\n\ntopUpVisitors(): deficit = targetOccupancy - countPresent(); for visitor agents with state AWAY or GONE → re-roll arrivalTime = now + randInt(0,6), visitDuration, state='AWAY'; break when deficit reached. Note: they must be spawned when their arrival time passes — the update loop handles spawn when simMinute >= arrivalTime ✓ (with jitter). Since arrival is 0-6 minutes ahead and at 120x that's ~3 real seconds... fine.\n\nHmm, but \"state = AWAY\" for a visitor who is currently present? No, only for AWAY/GONE ones.\n\nCareful: topUp sets state='AWAY' which triggers spawn in updateAgent when simMinute >= arrivalTime ✓.\n\nNow `applyOccupancy()`: for each agent, flip DISABLED <-> AWAY based on id < targetOccupancy; agents mid-workday left running (only park DISABLED if currently AWAY or GONE). Implement:\n```js\nfunction applyOccupancy() {\n  for (const agent of agents) {\n     if (agent.id < targetOccupancy) {\n        if (agent.state === 'DISABLED') { agent.state = 'AWAY'; }   // re-armed; will spawn at its arrival time\n     } else {\n        if (agent.state === 'AWAY' || agent.state === 'GONE') agent.state = 'DISABLED';\n     }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNow HUD. Build:\n```html\n<div id=\"hud\"> ... </div>\n```\nCreate via document.createElement in JS ✓.\n\nSpeed slider: log-spaced stops [1,2,4,8,16,30,60,120,240,400,600]; input range 0..10 value index of 120 → 7.\n\nOccupancy slider 1..100 default 45.\n\nBreakdown: counts per state + elevator info. Update throttled every ~0.3 real seconds.\n\nLighting keyframes: define array with hour anchors:\n```js\nconst DAY_KEYS = [\n {h:0, bg:0x1a2030, sunColor:0x2b3550, sunI:0.15, ai:0.45, hi:0.32},\n {h:5.5, ...},\n {h:6.0, dawn start...},\n {h:6.5, day...},\n ...\n];\n```\nShape: long flat daytime; narrow golden hour at 6-6:30 and 17:30-18:30. Night ambient ~0.45, hemi ~0.32.\n\nLet me define keys:\n- 0.0 night: bg #1a2030, sunColor #39435c, sunI 0.25, ai 0.45, hi 0.32\n- 5.8 night: same\n- 6.0 golden dawn start: bg #2f3a4e, sun #ff9a4d, sunI 0.5, ai 0.45, hi 0.32\n- 6.3 day: bg #20242a? Hmm daytime background should be brighter sky-ish: #2b3c52? Let's use daytime bg #2f4d68 with sun white intensity 1.0, ai 0.5, hi 0.45.\n- 17.3 day (same)\n- 17.5 golden dusk start: bg #3a3550, sun #ffb066, sunI 0.85, ai 0.46, hi 0.36\n- 18.5 night: bg #1a2030, sun #39435c, sunI 0.25, ai 0.45, hi 0.32\n\nInterpolate between keys (linear in hour). Good enough with compressed transitions.\n\nNow writing sim.js. Also `window` exports? Not required for sim.js but harmless.\n\nLet me write it now, carefully.\n\nOne more consideration: agents' groups added to scene directly; when in car, parent = elevator.carGroup ✓ collision check uses group.parent === elevator.carGroup.\n\nFor collisions \"agents sharing the same parent within ~1 unit of Y and ~0.7 XZ\" — implement using world positions? Use local positions relative to parent (same parent → comparable) ✓. I'll use group.position (local) since same parent.\n\nPush scalar 0.18: move each by half? Implement: for pair, if d < 0.7 and |dy|<1: push = 0.18 * (0.7 - d)/0.7 ... spec says low push scalar ~0.18. I'll do `const amount = 0.18 * motionDt * something`? Hmm, \"Use a low push scalar (~0.18) so a walking agent can still make progress past a stationary body.\" Let me implement: displacement per frame = dir * (0.7 - d) * 0.18 * ... Actually simplest: each agent moves by `dir * 0.18 * dtFactor` where dtFactor scales with motionDt but capped to avoid huge jumps at high timeScale. Use `const pushScalar = Math.min(0.35, 0.18 * motionDt)` hmm at 120x and realDt 0.016 → motionDt=1.92 → 0.345 per frame — that's big but fine (fast-forward). Cap at 0.3.\n\nLet me implement: `const push = Math.min(0.3, 0.18 * motionDt) * ((0.7 - d) / 0.7);` each agent moves half of separation? I'll move both by push*dir/2... Actually to avoid double counting, move each by dir*push/2 where dir points from a to b (a pushed backwards).\n\nHandle d < 1e-3: pick random separation direction ✓.\n\nSkip sitting agents and car agents and ENTER_ELEVATOR agents ✓. Also skip DISABLED/GONE/not-in-scene.\n\nAlso don't push agents outside the building? Not needed.\n\nNow, one more important behavior: agents walking must not walk through the shaft walls — BFS graph handles routing; but collision pushes may shove them into walls. Acceptable.\n\nLet me write sim.js.\n\nFor HUD state breakdown, states list.\n\nI'll now write the file.\n\nAdditional detail for `planVisitorVisit` weights per spec:\n- 10% bistro table (cafe)\n- 6% cafe counter\n- 14% front lounge\n- 12% back lounge / conversation pit\n- 10% reception/kiosk/water cooler (stand briefly)\n- 10% lobby loiter\n- 15% ride up to office-floor lounge\n- 23% sit in on a meeting\n\nTotal = 10+6+14+12+10+10+15+23 = 90%. Hmm, that's 90; add remaining 10% as \"visit a worker / stand at reception\"? The spec says roughly-tuned weights. I'll normalize by using cumulative weights summing to 100 with the listed values scaled: use exactly those and give the remaining 10% to \"lobby loiter\" (making it 20)? Better: implement weighted pick with these numbers as given, and treat leftover 10% as an extra \"chat at a coworker's desk on an office floor\" — but visitors have no desk; I'll add 'stand near reception' etc. Simplest: weights array summing to 90 plus 10 for \"conversation pit\"? Let me just define weights that total 100 by adding 10% to lobby loiter (20%) and note it in a comment. Hmm, spec explicitly lists ~10% loiter. I'll add the missing 10% as \"water cooler stand\" within the reception/kiosk/cooler bucket (making it 20)? That changes proportions too.\n\nAlternative: use weights as listed and normalize by total (90) — mathematically equivalent to proportional choice ✓. I'll do that with a comment noting normalization. Good.\n\nNow writing. Let me also handle `visitDuration` field for visitors.\n\nLet me write the code.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now `sim.js` — clock, agents, schedules, dispatch loop, collisions, HUD."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"lmstudio","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-gsq-rco","usage":{"input":81667,"output":7210,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7187,"totalTokens":88877,"cost":{"input":0,"