{"type":"compaction_end","reason":"threshold","result":{"summary":"No prior history.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\n- Implement a browser-only 3D office-building simulation using Three.js `0.147.0` from CDN, with no build process and no ES modules in browser files.\n- Required files:\n  - `person.js`\n  - `world.js`\n  - `elevator_logic.js`\n  - `elevator.js`\n  - `sim.js`\n  - `elevator_logic_test.js`\n  - `index.html`\n- The simulation must show a day in the life of a small office: agents arrive, work at desks, meet, lounge, eat lunch, leave around evening, and use a realistic elevator with call buttons, direction handling, capacity limits, doors, indicators, and scheduling.\n- Emphasis is behavioral fidelity, especially avoiding people bunching up, blocking entrances/elevators, sitting backwards on chairs, or failing to cross the front-door threshold.\n- Hard browser requirements:\n  - No top-level `import`/`export` in browser simulation files.\n  - Use explicit `window` globals for shared APIs.\n  - `elevator_logic.js` is dual-environment via IIFE and `module.exports`.\n  - `sim.js` must auto-start on page load with the required DOMContentLoaded pattern.\n  - Zero startup console errors.\n  - Run `node ../../static_check.js .` and, if available, `node ../../runtime_check.js .`.\n  - Must render a visible nonblank Three.js scene before complex behavior is added.\n  - No self-embedding, no `file://` URLs, no local absolute paths.\n  - Shared identifiers must be consistently spelled and not duplicated across classic scripts.\n\n## Progress So Far\n- Inspected the workspace:\n  - Workspace directory was empty except logs.\n  - Checker scripts are available two directories above.\n  - Playwright is available for runtime checks.\n- Created `person.js`:\n  - Defines `createPerson({bodyColor?, skinColor?, legColor?})`.\n  - Person origin is at feet, local `y = 0`.\n  - Legs pivot at hips, arms pivot at shoulders.\n  - Adds a nose hemisphere on the `+Z` face for facing direction.\n  - Defines `animatePersonWalking(person, dt)` with sitting/walking/idle limb animation.\n  - Exposes `window.createPerson` and `window.animatePersonWalking`.\n- Created `elevator_logic.js`:\n  - Pure Node-compatible elevator state machine using IIFE.\n  - States: `IDLE`, `MOVING`, `DOOR_OPENING`, `DOOR_OPEN`, `DOOR_CLOSING`.\n  - Public API includes `callUp`, `callDown`, `pressDestination`, `isAcceptingAt`, `currentCapacityFree`, `reserveBoardingSpot`, `completeBoard`, `registerDisembark`, `completeDisembark`, `tick`, and `reset`.\n  - Implements SCAN scheduling, direction handling, anti-starvation guards, door hold logic, safety cap, spot occupancy, and destination preservation.\n- Created `elevator_logic_test.js`:\n  - Deterministic Node tests using only `assert`.\n  - Required scenarios include lobby rush, destinations outranking same-floor calls, repeated hall-call starvation, opposite-direction calls waiting, door hold/safety cap, destination handshake, and reset clearing phantom state.\n- Fixed logic/test issues:\n  - Corrected internal method calls in `ElevatorLogic` to use `this.scanAhead(...)`.\n  - Adjusted test helper so “door closed” means the state machine has picked a next target (`MOVING` or `IDLE`).\n  - Added missing `pressDestination` step in the destination handshake test.\n  - Reworked lobby-rush test assertions to ensure passenger destinations are served before returning to floor 0.\n- Ran `node elevator_logic_test.js`:\n  - All seven tests pass: `7 passed, 0 failed`.\n\n## Context Needed to Continue\n- Remaining files still need to be created or completed:\n  - `world.js`\n  - `elevator.js`\n  - `sim.js`\n  - `index.html`\n- Must run required checkers before finishing:\n  - `node ../../static_check.js .`\n  - If Playwright is available, `node ../../runtime_check.js .`\n- Important coordinate conventions:\n  - `+Y` is up.\n  - `+Z` is front/entrance side; elevator doors face `+Z`.\n  - Floor `N` walkable floor is at `y = N * FLOOR_HEIGHT`.\n  - Shaft is a `3x3` column centered at `x=0, z=0`.\n  - Floor `0` is lobby; floors `1..5` are identical office floors.\n- Required world constants:\n  ```js\n  const WORLD = {\n      FLOOR_HEIGHT: 3.4,\n      FLOOR_COUNT: 6,\n      BUILDING_WIDTH: 22,\n      BUILDING_DEPTH: 18,\n      SHAFT_WIDTH: 3,\n      SHAFT_DEPTH: 3,\n      PERSON_R: 0.4\n  };\n  ```\n- Required world behavior:\n  - Semi-transparent building materials with `depthWrite: false` and `DoubleSide`.\n  - Building `renderOrder = 0`; elevator car meshes `renderOrder = 1`.\n  - Floor slabs are strips around the shaft opening.\n  - Front wall on floor 0 must have a real physical entrance gap at least 3 units wide centered on `x=0`.\n  - Navigation graph must include:\n    ```text\n    outside -> front_door_threshold -> entrance -> lobby_center\n    ```\n  - Hallway ring nodes required per floor:\n    ```text\n    hallS, hallSE, hallE, hallNE, hallN, hallNW, hallW, hallSW\n    elevWait\n    ```\n  - Call panels need `setUp`, `setDown`, and `setIndicator`.\n  - Canvas-texture indicators must cache `_lastText` to avoid re-uploading every frame.\n- Required elevator visual adapter:\n  - Class name must be `Elevator`.\n  - Must instantiate `new ElevatorLogic(...)` and delegate scheduling/state decisions to it.\n  - Must mirror logic state for HUD display.\n  - Must update car position, sliding doors, call-panel lamps, destination buttons, and floor indicators on each tick.\n- Required simulation behavior:\n  - Simulated clock starts at `07:30`.\n  - Default time scale is `120x` realtime.\n  - Motion must advance in lockstep with sim time using `motionDt = realDt * timeScale`.\n  - Day-wrap past midnight must reset agents and elevator completely.\n  - Agents include workers and visitors, with dynamic visitor top-up during business hours.\n  - Action dispatch must loop within one frame to avoid gaps that close doors on passengers.\n  - Collision handling must skip sit